    "global index": "ArcMMLU_26",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A File size of 500,000bytes, MSS equals 1000bytes. When we want to transmit this file with TCP, the sequence number of the first segment is 0, and the sequence number of the second segment is( ) \n\nOptions: \nA. 1000\nB. 999\nC. 1001\nD. 500000\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The question describes transmitting a file using TCP. Each segment carries a certain amount of data, and the sequence number of the next segment indicates the *next byte to be sent*. MSS (Maximum Segment Size) is the maximum amount of data a TCP segment can carry.\n\nThe first segment starts with sequence number 0. If the MSS is 1000 bytes, the first segment will carry 1000 bytes of data (or less, if it's the last segment and the remaining data is less than 1000 bytes). Therefore, the sequence number of the *first byte* in the second segment will be the sequence number of the first byte of the first segment plus the number of bytes sent in the first segment.\n\nSequence number of the first byte of the first segment = 0\nNumber of bytes in the first segment = MSS = 1000 bytes\nSequence number of the first byte of the second segment = 0 + 1000 = 1000\n\nThe correct answer is therefore 1000.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{A}$.",
