    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef replace_question_marks(s: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n\tGiven a string s representing a 12-hour format time where some of the digits (possibly none) are replaced with a \"?\",\n\treplace all the \"?\" characters in s with digits such that the time we obtain by the resulting string is a valid 12-hour format time and is the latest possible.\n\t\n\tArgs:\n\t\ts: A string representing a 12-hour format time with '?' characters.\n\n\tReturns:\n\t\tThe resulting string with '?' characters replaced to form the latest possible valid 12-hour time.\n\t\"\"\"\n    \n    result = list(s)\n\n    # Hour part\n    if result[0] == '?':\n        result[0] = '1'  # To make it the latest, start with '1'\n    if result[1] == '?':\n        # If the first digit is '1', the second digit can be at most '1' for '11'\n        # Otherwise, it can be '9'\n        if result[0] == '1':\n            result[1] = '1'\n        else:\n            result[1] = '9'\n\n    # Minute part\n    if result[3] == '?':\n        result[3] = '5'  # To make it the latest, set minutes to '5x'\n    if result[4] == '?':\n        result[4] = '9'  # To make it the latest, set minutes to 'x9'\n    \n    return \"\".join(result)\n```",
