      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    N, M, K = map(int, sys.stdin.readline().split())\n    edges = []\n    for _ in range(M):\n        u, v, w = map(int, sys.stdin.readline().split())\n        edges.append((u - 1, v - 1, w % K)) # Store weights modulo K directly\n\n    min_cost = float('inf')\n\n    # Iterate through all possible subsets of edges\n    # A spanning tree needs N-1 edges\n    from itertools import combinations\n    for spanning_tree_edges_indices in combinations(range(M), N - 1):\n        current_cost = 0\n        \n        # Check if the wybrany edges form a valid spanning tree\n        \n        # kruskal's algorithm to check for cycles\n        def find(parent, i):\n            if parent[i] == i:\n                return i\n            parent[i] = find(parent, parent[i])\n            return parent[i]\n\n        def union(parent, rank, x, y):\n            x_root = find(parent, x)\n            y_root = find(parent, y)\n\n            if x_root == y_root:\n                return False # Cycle detected\n            \n            if rank[x_root] < rank[y_root]:\n                parent[x_root] = y_root\n            elif rank[x_root] > rank[y_root]:\n                parent[y_root] = x_root\n            else:\n                parent[y_root] = x_root\n                rank[x_root] += 1\n            return True # Successfully united\n        \n        parent = [i for i in range(N)]\n        rank = [0] * N\n        num_edges_in_mst = 0\n        \n        is_spanning_tree = True\n        for i in spanning_tree_edges_indices:\n            u, v, w = edges[i]\n            if not union(parent, rank, u, v):\n                is_spanning_tree = False\n                break\n            current_cost = (current_cost + w) % K\n            num_edges_in_mst += 1\n            \n        if is_spanning_tree and num_edges_in_mst == N - 1:\n            # Check if all vertices are connected.\n            # If `num_edges_in_mst == N - 1` and all edges were successfully united\n            # (no cycles detected), then all N vertices must be in the same component.\n            # This is implicitly checked by the union-find structure: \n            # if we successfully added N-1 edges without creating a cycle, \n            # and there are N vertices, it must be a tree.\n            min_cost = min(min_cost, current_cost)\n\n    print(min_cost)\n\nsolve()\n```",
