      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef count_right_triangles(grid):\n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    count = 0\n\n    # Precompute the number of 1s in each row and column\n    row_ones = [0] * rows\n    col_ones = [0] * cols\n\n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            if grid[r][c] == 1:\n                row_ones[r] += 1\n                col_ones[c] += 1\n\n    # Iterate through each cell\n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            # If the current cell is a '1', it can be the corner of a right triangle\n            if grid[r][c] == 1:\n                # The number of right triangles with (r, c) as the corner\n                # is (number of 1s in row r - 1) * (number of 1s in col c - 1)\n                # We subtract 1 because we exclude the corner cell itself from the other two points\n                if row_ones[r] > 1 and col_ones[c] > 1:\n                    count += (row_ones[r] - 1) * (col_ones[c] - 1)\n\n    return count\n```",
