      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport bisect\n\ndef solve():\n    W, H = map(int, input().split())\n    N = int(input())\n    strawberries = []\n    for _ in range(N):\n        strawberries.append(list(map(int, input().split())))\n    A = int(input())\n    a = list(map(int, input().split()))\n    B = int(input())\n    b = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\n    # Add boundaries to cuts for easier bisecting\n    a_cuts = [0] + a + [W]\n    b_cuts = [0] + b + [H]\n\n    # Count strawberries in each piece\n    # A dictionary where keys are (x_interval_index, y_interval_index)\n    # and values are the number of strawberries in that piece.\n    piece_counts = {}\n\n    for px, py in strawberries:\n        # Find which x-interval this strawberry belongs to\n        # bisect_right gives the index of the first element > px\n        # Subtract 1 to get the index of the interval\n        x_idx = bisect.bisect_right(a_cuts, px) - 1\n        y_idx = bisect.bisect_right(b_cuts, py) - 1\n        piece_counts[(x_idx, y_idx)] = piece_counts.get((x_idx, y_idx), 0) + 1\n\n    # Calculate minimum and maximum\n    min_strawberries = float('inf')\n    max_strawberries = 0\n\n    # The total number of pieces is (A+1) * (B+1)\n    total_pieces = (A + 1) * (B + 1)\n\n    # Initialize min_strawberries if there are any pieces without strawberries\n    if len(piece_counts) < total_pieces:\n        min_strawberries = 0\n\n    for count in piece_counts.values():\n        min_strawberries = min(min_strawberries, count)\n        max_strawberries = max(max_strawberries, count)\n\n    # If there were no strawberries, all pieces have 0\n    if N == 0:\n        min_strawberries = 0\n        max_strawberries = 0\n\n    # If min_strawberries is still infinity, it means there were no pieces with 0 strawberries\n    # and we have accounted for all pieces that have strawberries.\n    # In this case, the minimum is the smallest count found.\n    if min_strawberries == float('inf'):\n        if piece_counts:\n            min_strawberries = min(piece_counts.values())\n        else: # This case should not happen given N>=1 and no strawberries on cuts\n            min_strawberries = 0\n\n    print(min_strawberries, max_strawberries)\n\n\ndef main():\n    solve()\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
