      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef max_length_substring(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Given a string s, return the maximum length of a substring such that it contains at most two occurrences of each character.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(s)\n    max_len = 0\n    # Iterate through all possible start points of a substring\n    for i in range(n):\n        # Keep track of character counts within the current substring\n        char_counts = {}\n        # Iterate through all possible end points of a substring starting at i\n        for j in range(i, n):\n            char = s[j]\n            char_counts[char] = char_counts.get(char, 0) + 1\n\n            # Check if the current substring is valid (at most two occurrences of each character)\n            is_valid = True\n            for count in char_counts.values():\n                if count > 2:\n                    is_valid = False\n                    break\n\n            # If the substring is valid, update the maximum length\n            if is_valid:\n                max_len = max(max_len, j - i + 1)\n            else:\n                # If the substring becomes invalid, no need to extend it further from this start point\n                break\n    return max_len\n```",
