    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef minOperationsDA(word: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the minimum number of operations to remove all adjacent almost-equal characters from a string.\n\n    Args:\n        word: The input string consisting of lowercase English letters.\n\n    Returns:\n        The minimum number of operations required.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(word)\n    operations = 0\n    i = 0\n    while i < n - 1:\n        char1 = word[i]\n        char2 = word[i + 1]\n\n        if char1 == char2:\n            operations += 1\n            i += 2  # Skip the next character as it's now considered handled\n        elif abs(ord(char1) - ord(char2)) == 1:\n            operations += 1\n            i += 2  # Skip the next character as it's now considered handled\n        else:\n            i += 1\n    return operations\n```",
