      "generated_answer": "Certainly! Below is the Python function that solves the problem as described in the prompt:\n\n```python\ndef minCoinsToAcquireFruits(prices):\n    n = len(prices)\n    total_coins = 0\n    i = 0\n    \n    while i < n:\n        total_coins += prices[i]\n        # Skip the next i fruits since they can be taken for free\n        i += i + 1\n    \n    return total_coins\n\n# Example usage:\n# prices = [3, 1, 2]\n# print(minCoinsToAcquireFruits(prices))  # Output: 4\n```\n\nThis function calculates the minimum number of coins needed to acquire all the fruits from the market. It does so by iterating over the prices array and taking advantage of the offer that allows multiple fruits to be acquired for free. The key is to strategically choose which fruits to purchase such that the sum of the costs is minimized.",
