      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    s = sys.stdin.readline().strip()\n    n = len(s)\n\n    # Iterate through all possible split points for S_A, S_B, and S_C\n    for i in range(n + 1):  # i is the length of S_A\n        for j in range(n - i + 1):  # j is the length of S_B\n            k = n - i - j  # k is the length of S_C\n\n            # Extract the potential substrings\n            s_a = s[:i]\n            s_b = s[i:i+j]\n            s_c = s[i+j:]\n\n            # Check if s_a is an A string\n            is_a_string = all(char == 'A' for char in s_a)\n            if len(s_a) > 0 and not is_a_string:\n                continue\n\n            # Check if s_b is a B string\n            is_b_string = all(char == 'B' for char in s_b)\n            if len(s_b) > 0 and not is_b_string:\n                continue\n\n            # Check if s_c is a C string\n            is_c_string = all(char == 'C' for char in s_c)\n            if len(s_c) > 0 and not is_c_string:\n                continue\n\n            # If all conditions are met, it's an Extended ABC string\n            print(\"Yes\")\n            return\n\n    # If no such split is found after checking all possibilities\n    print(\"No\")\n\n\ndef main():\n    solve()\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
