      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef solve():\n    N = int(input())\n\n    # The minimum number of friends M needed is ceil(log2(N)).\n    # This is because each friend's outcome (sick or not sick) gives us one bit of information.\n    # To distinguish between N possibilities, we need at least log2(N) bits.\n    M = math.ceil(math.log2(N))\n    print(M)\n\n    friend_bottles = [[] for _ in range(M)]\n\n    # We use a binary encoding approach.\n    # For each bottle i (from 1 to N), its binary representation will determine\n    # which friends receive it.\n    # If the k-th bit of i is 1, then bottle i is given to friend k.\n    for i in range(1, N + 1):\n        # Convert bottle number (i) to its binary representation\n        # We need M bits, so pad with leading zeros if necessary\n        binary_i = bin(i - 1)[2:].zfill(M) # i-1 because we want 0-indexed binary for M friends\n\n        for j in range(M):\n            if binary_i[M - 1 - j] == '1': # Check the j-th bit from the right\n                friend_bottles[j].append(i)\n\n    for i in range(M):\n        line = [str(len(friend_bottles[i]))] + [str(b) for b in friend_bottles[i]]\n        print(\" \".join(line))\n\n    S = input()\n\n    spoiled_binary_str = \"\"\n    for char_s in S:\n        spoiled_binary_str += char_s\n\n    # Convert the binary string from S back to an integer\n    # This represents the 0-indexed spoiled bottle.\n    spoiled_bottle_0_indexed = int(spoiled_binary_str, 2)\n\n    # Convert back to 1-indexed bottle number\n    spoiled_bottle = spoiled_bottle_0_indexed + 1\n\n    print(spoiled_bottle)\n\nsolve()\n```",
