    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef furthest_distance(moves: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the furthest distance from the origin achievable given a string of moves.\n\n    Args:\n        moves: A string consisting of 'L', 'R', and '_' representing possible moves.\n\n    Returns:\n        The absolute distance from the origin of the furthest point reachable.\n    \"\"\"\n    left_moves = 0\n    right_moves = 0\n    unknown_moves = 0\n\n    for move in moves:\n        if move == 'L':\n            left_moves += 1\n        elif move == 'R':\n            right_moves += 1\n        else:\n            unknown_moves += 1\n\n    # To maximize the distance to the left, we assume all '_' are moves to the left.\n    # To maximize the distance to the right, we assume all '_' are moves to the right.\n    # The furthest distance will be the maximum of these two scenarios.\n\n    furthest_left = left_moves + unknown_moves\n    furthest_right = right_moves + unknown_moves\n\n    return max(furthest_left, furthest_right)\n```",
