      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\nsys.setrecursionlimit(10**6)\n\nmemo = {}\n\ndef solve():\n    N, A, X, Y = map(int, sys.stdin.readline().split())\n\n    def get_min_expected_cost(n):\n        if n == 0:\n            return 0.0\n        if n == 1:\n            return min(X, Y * (6 / 5)) # If die rolls 1, N remains 1. Otherwise, N becomes 0. So need 6/5 expected rolls to get something other than 1\n        if n in memo:\n            return memo[n]\n\n        # Option 1: Pay X yen to replace N with floor(N/A)\n        cost_option1 = X + get_min_expected_cost(n // A)\n\n        # Option 2: Pay Y yen to roll a die\n        # Expected cost = Y + sum(P(b) * get_min_expected_cost(n // b)) for b in [1, 6]\n        # P(b) = 1/6 for each b\n        expected_cost_option2 = Y\n        for b in range(2, 7): # N becomes 0 if b >= N (which means n//b becomes 0 if b >= N)\n             expected_cost_option2 += (1/6) * get_min_expected_cost(n // b)\n\n        # Special handling for b=1: N remains N.\n        # Let E be the expected cost for current N.\n        # E = Y + (1/6)E + (1/6) * sum(expected_cost(n//b)) for b=2 to 6\n        # (5/6)E = Y + (1/6) * sum(expected_cost(n//b)) for b=2 to 6\n        # E = (6/5) * (Y + (1/6) * sum(expected_cost(n//b)) for b=2 to 6)\n        # E = (6/5) * Y + (1/5) * sum(expected_cost(n//b)) for b=2 to 6\n        \n        # Recalculate this based on the definition:\n        # E_N = Y + (1/6)E_N + (1/6)E_{N//2} + ... + (1/6)E_{N//6}\n        # (5/6)E_N = Y + (1/6)Sum_{b=2 to 6} (E_{N//b})\n        # E_N = (6/5)Y + (1/5)Sum_{b=2 to 6} (E_{N//b})\n        \n        expected_cost_option2_sum_part = 0.0\n        for b in range(2, 7):\n            expected_cost_option2_sum_part += get_min_expected_cost(n // b)\n        \n        cost_option2 = (6/5) * Y + (1/5) * expected_cost_option2_sum_part\n\n\n        result = min(cost_option1, cost_option2)\n        memo[n] = result\n        return result\n\n    print(f\"{get_min_expected_cost(N):.15f}\")\n\nsolve()\n```",
