2: Replace '?' with a lowercase letter\n            if char == '?' or ('a' <= char <= 'z'):\n                current_char_options = 1 if char != '?' else 26\n                for k in range(current_char_options):\n                    lower_char = 'a' if char == '?' else char\n                    if j == 2: # From \"AA\"\n                        dp[i + 1][3] = (dp[i + 1][3] + dp[i][j]) % MOD\n                    elif j == 3: # From \"AAa\"\n                        # If the current lowercase letter is the same as 'a', it continues the \"AAa\" prefix.\n                        # We don't transition to a new state based on this.\n                        pass\n                    elif j == 4: # Already have a DDoS-type subsequence\n                        dp[i + 1][4] = (dp[i + 1][4] + dp[i][j]) % MOD\n\n    # The answer is the number of strings that do not contain a DDoS-type subsequence.\n    # This is the total number of valid strings minus those that form a DDoS-type subsequence.\n    # However, our DP is designed to count those that *do not* form a DDoS-type subsequence\n    # by stopping the counts at state 4.\n    # So, the number of valid strings is the sum of dp[n][0], dp[n][1], and dp[n][2], dp[n][3].\n    # The state 4 is the \"forbidden\" state.\n    ans = (dp[n][0] + dp[n][1] + dp[n][2] + dp[n][3]) % MOD\n    print(ans)\n\ndef main():\n    solve()\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
