0, 1, and 2. Among these, the answer is the string at index 2 because it has the shortest length of 6.\nFor wordsQuery[1] = \"acbfgh\", only the string at index 0 shares the longest common suffix \"fgh\". Hence it is the answer, even though the string at index 2 is shorter.\nFor wordsQuery[2] = \"acbfegh\", strings from wordsContainer that share the longest common suffix \"gh\" are at indices 0, 1, and 2. Among these, the answer is the string at index 2 because it has the shortest length of 6.\n\n\n \nConstraints:\n\n1 <= wordsContainer.length, wordsQuery.length <= 10^4\n1 <= wordsContainer[i].length <= 5 * 10^3\n1 <= wordsQuery[i].length <= 5 * 10^3\nwordsContainer[i] consists only of lowercase English letters.\nwordsQuery[i] consists only of lowercase English letters.\nSum of wordsContainer[i].length is at most 5 * 10^5.\nSum of wordsQuery[i].length is at most 5 * 10^5.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef findLongestCommonSuffix(wordsContainer, wordsQuery):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the index of the string in wordsContainer that has the longest common suffix\n    with each string in wordsQuery, with tie-breaking rules.\n\n    Args:\n        wordsContainer: A list of strings.\n        wordsQuery: A list of strings.\n\n    Returns:\n        A list of integers, where ans[i] is the index of the best matching string\n        in wordsContainer for wordsQuery[i].\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(wordsContainer)\n    m = len(wordsQuery)\n    ans = [-1] * m\n\n    # Precompute reversed words and a trie for efficient suffix searching\n    reversed_container = [word[::-1] for word in wordsContainer]\n    \n    trie = {}\n    for i, word in enumerate(reversed_container):\n        node = trie\n        for char in word:\n            if char not in node:\n                node[char] = {}\n            node = node[char]\n            # Store (length, index) at each node to track best candidate\n            if 'best' not in node:\n                node['best'] = (len(word), i)\n            else:\n                current_best_len, current_best_idx = node['best']\n                if len(word) < current_best_len:\n                    node['best'] = (len(word), i)\n                elif len(word) == current_best_len and i < current_best_idx:\n                    node['best'] = (len(word), i)\n\n    for i, query_word in enumerate(wordsQuery):\n        reversed_query = query_word[::-1]\n        node = trie\n        best_match_len = 0\n        best_match_idx = -1\n        \n        # Track the best candidate encountered so far from trie traversal\n        initial_best_candidate = (-1, -1) # (length, index)\n        \n        for char in reversed_query:\n            if char in node:\n                node = node[char]\n                if 'best' in node:\n                    current_candidate_len, current_candidate_idx = node['best']\n                    \n                    # Compare with the overall best candidate found in this query\n                    if initial_best_candidate == (-1, -1):\n                        initial_best_candidate = node['best']\n                    else:\n                        prev_best_len, prev_best_idx = initial_best_candidate\n                        if current_candidate_len < prev_best_len:\n                            initial_best_candidate = node['best']\n                        elif current_candidate_len == prev_best_len and current_candidate_idx < prev_best_idx:\n                            initial_best_candidate = node['best']\n            else:\n                break\n                \n        # If no common suffix found, the best match is the one with the smallest length\n        # among all container words. If multiple have the same smallest length, pick the\n        # earliest occurring one.\n        if initial_best_candidate == (-1, -1):\n            overall_best_len = float('inf')\n            overall_best_idx = -1\n            for idx, word in enumerate(wordsContainer):\n                if len(word) < overall_best_len:\n                    overall_best_len = len(word)\n                    overall_best_idx = idx\n                elif len(word) == overall_best_len and idx < overall_best_idx:\n                    overall_best_idx = idx\n            ans[i] = overall_best_idx\n        else:\n            ans[i] = initial_best_candidate[1]\n\n    return ans\n```",
