      "generated_answer": "```python\nfrom collections import Counter\n\ndef solve():\n    S = input()\n    T = input()\n\n    matching_chars = set(['a', 't', 'c', 'o', 'd', 'e', 'r'])\n\n    count_s = Counter(S)\n    count_t = Counter(T)\n\n    can_win = True\n\n    for char_code in range(ord('a'), ord('z') + 1):\n        char = chr(char_code)\n        if char == '@':\n            continue\n\n        s_count = count_s.get(char, 0)\n        t_count = count_t.get(char, 0)\n\n        if s_count == t_count:\n            continue\n        elif char in matching_chars:\n            if s_count > t_count:\n                diff = s_count - t_count\n                if count_t.get('@', 0) >= diff:\n                    count_t['@'] -= diff\n                else:\n                    can_win = False\n                    break\n            else: # t_count > s_count\n                diff = t_count - s_count\n                if count_s.get('@', 0) >= diff:\n                    count_s['@'] -= diff\n                else:\n                    can_win = False\n                    break\n        else: # character not in matching_chars and counts don't match\n            can_win = False\n            break\n\n    if can_win and count_s.get('@', 0) == count_t.get('@', 0):\n        print(\"Yes\")\n    else:\n        print(\"No\")\n\nsolve()\n```",
