    "prompt": "Generate an executable Python function generated from the given prompt. The function should take stdin as input and print the output. Simply call the function after the definition. Question:\nA string T of length 3 consisting of uppercase English letters is an airport code for a string S of lowercase English letters if and only if T can be derived from S by one of the following methods:\n\n- Take a subsequence of length 3 from S (not necessarily contiguous) and convert it to uppercase letters to form T.\n- Take a subsequence of length 2 from S (not necessarily contiguous), convert it to uppercase letters, and append X to the end to form T.\n\nGiven strings S and T, determine if T is an airport code for S.\n\nInput\n\nThe input is given from Standard Input in the following format:\nS\r\nT\n\nOutput\n\nPrint Yes if T is an airport code for S, and No otherwise.\n\nConstraints\n\n\n- S is a string of lowercase English letters with a length between 3 and 10^5, inclusive.\n- T is a string of uppercase English letters with a length of 3.\n\nSample Input 1\n\nnarita\r\nNRT\n\nSample Output 1\n\nYes\r\n\nThe subsequence nrt of narita, when converted to uppercase, forms the string NRT, which is an airport code for narita.\n\nSample Input 2\n\nlosangeles\r\nLAX\n\nSample Output 2\n\nYes\r\n\nThe subsequence la of losangeles, when converted to uppercase and appended with X, forms the string LAX, which is an airport code for losangeles.\n\nSample Input 3\n\nsnuke\r\nRNG\n\nSample Output 3\n\nNo",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef is_airport_code(S, T):\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if string T is an airport code for string S.\n\n    Args:\n        S: A string of lowercase English letters.\n        T: A string of uppercase English letters with a length of 3.\n\n    Returns:\n        \"Yes\" if T is an airport code for S, \"No\" otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # Method 1: Subsequence of length 3\n    def check_subsequence_3():\n        s_index = 0\n        t_index = 0\n        while s_index < len(S) and t_index < 3:\n            if S[s_index].upper() == T[t_index]:\n                t_index += 1\n            s_index += 1\n        return t_index == 3\n\n    # If method 1 works, return \"Yes\"\n    if check_subsequence_3():\n        return \"Yes\"\n\n    # Method 2: Subsequence of length 2 and append 'X'\n    if T[2] == 'X':\n        def check_subsequence_2_and_X():\n            subsequence = []\n            s_index = 0\n            t_index = 0\n            while s_index < len(S) and t_index < 2:\n                if S[s_index].upper() == T[t_index]:\n                    subsequence.append(S[s_index].upper())\n                    t_index += 1\n                s_index += 1\n            return t_index == 2\n\n        # If method 2 works, return \"Yes\"\n        if check_subsequence_2_and_X():\n            return \"Yes\"\n\n    # If neither method works, return \"No\"\n    return \"No\"\n\ndef main():\n    S = sys.stdin.readline().strip()\n    T = sys.stdin.readline().strip()\n    print(is_airport_code(S, T))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
