    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef find_difference(n: int, m: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the difference between the sum of integers not divisible by m and the sum of integers divisible by m within the range [1, n].\n\n    Args:\n        n: A positive integer representing the upper bound of the range.\n        m: A positive integer representing the divisor.\n\n    Returns:\n        The integer num1 - num2, where:\n        num1: The sum of all integers in the range [1, n] that are not divisible by m.\n        num2: The sum of all integers in the range [1, n] that are divisible by m.\n    \"\"\"\n    num1 = 0\n    num2 = 0\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        if i % m != 0:\n            num1 += i\n        else:\n            num2 += i\n    return num1 - num2\n```",
