      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef count_k_distance_pairs(coordinates, k):\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of pairs (i, j) such that i < j\n    and the distance between points i and j is equal to k.\n\n    Args:\n        coordinates: A 2D integer array where coordinates[i] = [x_i, y_i].\n        k: The target distance.\n\n    Returns:\n        The number of pairs (i, j) with the specified distance k.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(coordinates)\n    count = 0\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            x1, y1 = coordinates[i]\n            x2, y2 = coordinates[j]\n            distance = (x1 ^ x2) + (y1 ^ y2)\n            if distance == k:\n                count += 1\n    return count\n\n```",
