    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef canBeEqual(s1: str, s2: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if two strings of length 4 can be made equal by swapping characters\n    at indices i and j where j - i = 2.\n\n    Args:\n        s1: The first string.\n        s2: The second string.\n\n    Returns:\n        True if the strings can be made equal, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # Helper function to get all possible strings reachable from a given string\n    def get_reachable_strings(s):\n        reachable = set()\n        reachable.add(s)\n\n        # Initial state\n        q = [s]\n\n        while q:\n            current_s = q.pop(0)\n            \n            # Apply operations\n            for i in range(2):  # i = 0 or i = 1\n                j = i + 2\n                \n                # Create new string by swapping characters\n                s_list = list(current_s)\n                s_list[i], s_list[j] = s_list[j], s_list[i]\n                new_s = \"\".join(s_list)\n\n                if new_s not in reachable:\n                    reachable.add(new_s)\n                    q.append(new_s)\n        return reachable\n\n    # Get all possible strings reachable from s1\n    reachable_from_s1 = get_reachable_strings(s1)\n\n    # Check if s2 is in the set of reachable strings from s1\n    return s2 in reachable_from_s1\n```",
