    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport itertools\n\ndef solve():\n    H, W = map(int, input().split())\n    A = [list(map(int, input().split())) for _ in range(H)]\n    B = [list(map(int, input().split())) for _ in range(H)]\n\n    def get_cost(grid_a, grid_b):\n        original_rows = list(range(H))\n        original_cols = list(range(W))\n\n        min_ops = float('inf')\n\n        for row_perm in itertools.permutations(original_rows):\n            current_a_rows = [A[r] for r in row_perm]\n\n            # Check if row permutations alone can match B's rows\n            temp_a = [list(row) for row in current_a_rows]\n            row_ops = 0\n            for i in range(H):\n                if original_rows[i] != row_perm[i]:\n                    row_ops += 1\n                    original_rows[i], original_rows[original_rows.index(row_perm[i])] = original_rows[original_rows.index(row_perm[i])], original_rows[i]\n            row_ops = 0\n            for i in range(H - 1):\n                if row_perm[i] > row_perm[i+1]:\n                    row_perm[i], row_perm[i+1] = row_perm[i+1], row_perm[i]\n                    row_ops += 1\n\n\n            possible_col_perms = []\n            for col_perm in itertools.permutations(original_cols):\n                a_grid_permuted = [[temp_a[r][c] for c in col_perm] for r in range(H)]\n                if a_grid_permuted == grid_b:\n                    col_ops = 0\n                    current_col_order = list(range(W))\n                    for i in range(W - 1):\n                        if col_perm[i] > col_perm[i+1]:\n                            col_perm[i], col_perm[i+1] = col_perm[i+1], col_perm[i]\n                            col_ops += 1\n                    possible_col_perms.append(col_ops)\n\n            if possible_col_perms:\n                min_ops = min(min_ops, row_ops + min(possible_col_perms))\n\n        return min_ops if min_ops != float('inf') else float('inf')\n\n    min_total_ops = float('inf')\n\n    # Iterate through all possible row permutations for A\n    original_row_indices = list(range(H))\n    for row_permutation in itertools.permutations(original_row_indices):\n        temp_a_rows = [A[i] for i in row_permutation]\n        current_row_ops = 0\n        # Calculate row swap operations needed to reach this permutation\n        p = list(row_permutation)\n        for i in range(H - 1):\n            for j in range(i + 1, H):\n                if p[i] > p[j]:\n                    p[i], p[j] = p[j], p[i]\n                    current_row_ops += 1\n\n        # Now, for this fixed row permutation, try all column permutations\n        original_col_indices = list(range(W))\n        for col_permutation in itertools.permutations(original_col_indices):\n            current_a_permuted = [[temp_a_rows[r][c] for c in col_permutation] for r in range(H)]\n            if current_a_permuted == B:\n                current_col_ops = 0\n                # Calculate column swap operations needed to reach this permutation\n                q = list(col_permutation)\n                for i in range(W - 1):\n                    for j in range(i + 1, W):\n                        if q[i] > q[j]:\n                            q[i], q[j] = q[j], q[i]\n                            current_col_ops += 1\n                min_total_ops = min(min_total_ops, current_row_ops + current_col_ops)\n\n    if min_total_ops == float('inf'):\n        print(-1)\n    else:\n        print(min_total_ops)\n\nsolve()\n```",
