    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef solve():\n    N = int(input())\n    points = []\n    for i in range(N):\n        x, y = map(int, input().split())\n        points.append(((x, y), i + 1)) # Store coordinates and original ID\n\n    for i in range(N):\n        current_point_coords, current_point_id = points[i]\n        max_distance_sq = -1\n        farthest_point_id = -1\n\n        for j in range(N):\n            if i == j:\n                continue\n\n            other_point_coords, other_point_id = points[j]\n            \n            dx = current_point_coords[0] - other_point_coords[0]\n            dy = current_point_coords[1] - other_point_coords[1]\n            distance_sq = dx**2 + dy**2\n\n            if distance_sq > max_distance_sq:\n                max_distance_sq = distance_sq\n                farthest_point_id = other_point_id\n            elif distance_sq == max_distance_sq:\n                farthest_point_id = min(farthest_point_id, other_point_id)\n        \n        print(farthest_point_id)\n\nsolve()\n```",
