ls in a fixed row `r_mod = i % N`.\n                # Sum of black cells in row `i` from `c_start` to `c_end`:\n                # Number of full N-column segments in `[c_start, c_end]`: `num_N_seg_cols = (c_end + 1) // N - c_start // N`\n                # This would give `num_N_seg_cols * black_in_pattern_row[i % N]` if `c_start` and `c_end` were aligned with N-boundaries.\n\n                # Let's use the prefix sum approach on rows and columns for the infinite grid.\n                # `count_black_up_to(R, C)`: number of black cells in grid from (0, 0) to (R, C).\n\n                def count_black_up_to(R, C):\n                    if R < 0 or C < 0:\n                        return 0\n\n                    num_full_N_rows = (R + 1) // N\n                    num_full_N_cols = (C + 1) // N\n\n                    count_from_full_blocks = num_full_N_rows * num_full_N_cols * total_black_in_full_pattern\n\n                    # Contribution from partial columns in full N-row blocks\n                    # Rows 0 to num_full_N_rows * N - 1. Columns num_full_N_cols * N to C.\n                    # For each row `i` in range `[0, num_full_N_rows * N - 1]`, we sum `P[i % N][j % N]` for `j` in `[num_full_N_cols * N, C]`.\n                    # `j % N` will be in `[0, C % N]`.\n                    # The `i % N` will cycle through `0, 1, ..., N-1`.\n                    #\n                    # Contribution for columns `j` from `num_full_N_cols * N` to `C`:\n                    # The portion of columns is `[0, C % N]`.\n                    # For rows `i` from `0` to `num_full_N_rows * N - 1`:\n                    # The row modulo N part is `i % N`.\n                    #\n                    # For each row modulo `r_mod` from `0` to `N-1`:\n                    # How many times does row `r_mod` appear in rows `0` to `num_full_N_rows * N - 1`?\n                    # It appears `num_full_N_rows` times.\n                    #\n                    # So, for columns `j` in `[num_full_N