      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    N, L, R = map(int, input().split())\n\n    total_sum_mod_100 = 0\n\n    # Iterate through each bit position from N-1 down to 0\n    # This corresponds to block sizes 2^(N-1), 2^(N-2), ..., 2^0\n    for i in range(N - 1, -1, -1):\n        block_size = 1 << i\n\n        # Calculate the starting and ending blocks for the current block_size\n        start_block_idx = L // block_size\n        end_block_idx = R // block_size\n\n        # Case 1: L and R are within the same block of size block_size\n        if start_block_idx == end_block_idx:\n            # If the current block fully covers the range [L, R]\n            # (i.e., L is the start of the block and R is the end of the block),\n            # we need to query this block.\n            # Otherwise, this block is not fully contained, and we defer\n            # it to smaller block sizes.\n            if L % block_size == 0 and R % block_size == block_size - 1:\n                j = L // block_size\n                print(f\"? {i} {j}\", flush=True)\n                T = int(input())\n                if T == -1:\n                    exit()\n                total_sum_mod_100 = (total_sum_mod_100 + T) % 100\n                # Since we covered the entire range, we are done\n                break\n        else:\n            # Case 2: L and R span across multiple blocks of size block_size\n\n            # Handle the partial block at the beginning (containing L)\n            if L % block_size != 0:\n                # If L is not the start of a block of size block_size,\n                # we don't query this block directly. We rely on smaller blocks\n                # to cover the remainder of L.\n                pass\n            else:\n                # If L is the start of a block, query this block\n                j = start_block_idx\n                print(f\"? {i} {j}\", flush=True)\n                T = int(input())\n                if T == -1:\n                    exit()\n                total_sum_mod_100 = (total_sum_mod_100 + T) % 100\n                L += block_size\n\n            # Handle full blocks in between L and R\n            while L + block_size - 1 <= R - (R % block_size):\n                j = L // block_size\n                print(f\"? {i} {j}\", flush=True)\n                T = int(input())\n                if T == -1:\n                    exit()\n                total_sum_mod_100 = (total_sum_mod_100 + T) % 100\n                L += block_size\n\n            # Handle the partial block at the end (containing R)\n            # If R is not the end of a block of size block_size,\n            # we don't query this block directly. We rely on smaller blocks\n            # to cover the remainder of R.\n            if R % block_size != block_size - 1:\n                pass\n            else:\n                # If R is the end of a block, query this block\n                # This ensures we cover any full block ending at R that wasn't\n                # covered by the middle loop if R was exactly on a block boundary.\n                # Example: L=0, R=1 for N=2. i=1, block_size=2.\n                # L%2==0, so query ? 1 0. L becomes 2. Loop condition fails.\n                # But R is also 1, so R%2 == 1. This block contains R.\n                # This only executes if it's a full block of size `block_size`\n                # that also ends at R.\n                j = R // block_size\n                # We need to make sure this is not a block already covered\n                # This check ensures we don't query the same block again\n                # and only query it if it's the specific full block at R.\n                if L <= j * block_size:\n                    print(f\"? {i} {j}\", flush=True)\n                    T = int(input())\n                    if T == -1:\n                        exit()\n                    total_sum_mod_100 = (total_sum_mod_100 + T) % 100\n                    # Update R, but it's not strictly necessary as we break\n                    # after this loop.\n                    R = j * block_size - 1\n\n        # If L already passed R, we have covered all of [L_orig, R_orig]\n        if L > R:\n            break\n\n    print(f\"! {total_sum_mod_100}\", flush=True)\n\n\nsolve()\n```",
