    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef stableBinaryArrays(zero: int, one: int, limit: int) -> int:\n    MOD = 10**9 + 7\n\n    dp = {}\n\n    # dp((last_char, current_length_of_last_char_runs, remaining_zeros, remaining_ones)) returns the number of stable arrays\n    def solve(last_char, current_run_length, r_zeros, r_ones):\n        if (last_char, current_run_length, r_zeros, r_ones) in dp:\n            return dp[(last_char, current_run_length, r_zeros, r_ones)]\n\n        if r_zeros == 0 and r_ones == 0:\n            return 1\n\n        ans = 0\n\n        # Try appending a '0'\n        if last_char == 0:\n            if current_run_length < limit and r_zeros > 0:\n                ans = (ans + solve(0, current_run_length + 1, r_zeros - 1, r_ones)) % MOD\n            if r_ones > 0:\n                ans = (ans + solve(1, 1, r_zeros, r_ones - 1)) % MOD\n        else:  # last_char == 1\n            if r_zeros > 0:\n                ans = (ans + solve(0, 1, r_zeros - 1, r_ones)) % MOD\n            if current_run_length < limit and r_ones > 0:\n                ans = (ans + solve(1, current_run_length + 1, r_zeros, r_ones - 1)) % MOD\n\n        dp[(last_char, current_run_length, r_zeros, r_ones)] = ans\n        return ans\n\n    # Initialize dp table for memoization\n    dp = {}\n\n    # Start with '0'\n    ans_start_0 = solve(0, 1, zero - 1, one) if zero > 0 else 0\n    # Start with '1'\n    ans_start_1 = solve(1, 1, zero, one - 1) if one > 0 else 0\n    \n    return (ans_start_0 + ans_start_1) % MOD\n\n```",
