      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef punishmentNumber(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the punishment number of a given positive integer n.\n\n    The punishment number of n is defined as the sum of the squares of all integers i such that:\n    1 <= i <= n\n    The decimal representation of i * i can be partitioned into contiguous substrings such that the sum of the integer values of these substrings equals i.\n\n    Args:\n        n: A positive integer.\n\n    Returns:\n        The punishment number of n.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def can_partition_sum(s_num: str, target: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Helper function to check if the string representation of a number\n        can be partitioned into contiguous substrings that sum up to the target.\n        \"\"\"\n        \n        def backtrack(index: int, current_sum: int) -> bool:\n            if index == len(s_num):\n                return current_sum == target\n\n            for i in range(index, len(s_num)):\n                substring_val = int(s_num[index:i+1])\n                if current_sum + substring_val <= target:\n                    if backtrack(i + 1, current_sum + substring_val):\n                        return True\n            return False\n\n        return backtrack(0, 0)\n\n    punishment_sum = 0\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        i_squared = i * i\n        s_i_squared = str(i_squared)\n\n        if can_partition_sum(s_i_squared, i):\n            punishment_sum += i_squared\n            \n    return punishment_sum\n```",
