      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    L, R = map(int, input().split())\n\n    result = []\n    current_l = L\n\n    while current_l < R:\n        max_power_of_2 = 0\n        for i in range(61):  # 2^60 is max, so 60+1\n            if current_l % (1 << (i + 1)) == 0 and current_l + (1 << (i + 1)) <= R:\n                max_power_of_2 = i + 1\n            elif (current_l % (1 << (i + 1)) != 0 and current_l % (1 << i) == 0) and current_l + (1 << i) <= R:\n                max_power_of_2 = i\n                break\n            elif current_l % (1 << i) != 0 and (current_l + (1 << i) > R):\n                break\n            elif i == 0:\n                max_power_of_2 = i\n                break\n        \n        if (current_l >> max_power_of_2) % 2 == 0: # This means check if j is odd or even\n          # Case when current_l = 2^i * j, j is even\n          current_r = current_l + (1 << max_power_of_2)\n          result.append((current_l, current_r))\n          current_l = current_r\n        else:\n          # Case when current_l = 2^i * j, j is odd\n          j = current_l >> max_power_of_2\n          current_r = (j + 1) << max_power_of_2\n          if current_r > R:\n              k = 0\n              while True:\n                  if (current_l + (1 << k)) > R:\n                      break\n                  k += 1\n              current_r = current_l + (1 << (k-1))\n          result.append((current_l, current_r))\n          current_l = current_r\n        \n          \n    print(len(result))\n    for l, r in result:\n        print(l, r)\n\nsolve()\n```",
