    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef color_array(n: int, queries: list[list[int]]) -> list[int]:\n    nums = [0] * n\n    answer = []\n    current_same_color_pairs = 0\n\n    def check_and_update(idx, old_val, new_val, current_count):\n        count_change = 0\n        # Check left neighbor\n        if idx > 0:\n            if nums[idx - 1] == old_val and old_val != 0:\n                count_change -= 1\n            if nums[idx - 1] == new_val and new_val != 0:\n                count_change += 1\n        # Check right neighbor\n        if idx < n - 1:\n            if nums[idx + 1] == old_val and old_val != 0:\n                count_change -= 1\n            if nums[idx + 1] == new_val and new_val != 0:\n                count_change += 1\n        return current_count + count_change\n\n    for index_i, color_i in queries:\n        old_color = nums[index_i]\n\n        # Before updating, subtract contributions from old color\n        # Check left\n        if index_i > 0 and nums[index_i - 1] == old_color and old_color != 0:\n            current_same_color_pairs -= 1\n        # Check right\n        if index_i < n - 1 and nums[index_i + 1] == old_color and old_color != 0:\n            current_same_color_pairs -= 1\n\n        nums[index_i] = color_i\n\n        # After updating, add contributions from new color\n        # Check left\n        if index_i > 0 and nums[index_i - 1] == color_i and color_i != 0:\n            current_same_color_pairs += 1\n        # Check right\n        if index_i < n - 1 and nums[index_i + 1] == color_i and color_i != 0:\n            current_same_color_pairs += 1\n\n        answer.append(current_same_color_pairs)\n\n    return answer\n```",
