      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef greatest_integer(k: int, x: int) -> int:\n    def count_set_bits_at_position(num, pos, x):\n        if pos % x != 0:\n            return 0\n        count = 0\n        for i in range(pos, -1, -x):\n            block_size = 1 << (i + 1)\n            num_blocks = (num + 1) // block_size\n            count += num_blocks * ((1 << i) // 2)\n            remainder = (num + 1) % block_size\n            if remainder > (1 << i):\n                count += remainder - (1 << i)\n        return count\n\n    def calculate_total_price(num, x):\n        total_price = 0\n        max_bit = num.bit_length()\n        for i in range(1, max_bit + 1):\n            if i % x == 0:\n                total_price += count_set_bits_at_position(num, i - 1, x)\n        return total_price\n\n    left, right = 0, 2 * (10**15)  # A sufficiently large upper bound\n    ans = 0\n\n    while left <= right:\n        mid = (left + right) // 2\n        if mid == 0:  # Handle the case where mid is 0\n            left = 1\n            continue\n\n        current_sum_of_prices = 0\n        for i in range(1, 61):  # Iterate through bit positions up to a reasonable limit\n            if i % x == 0:\n                # Count numbers from 1 to mid that have the i-th bit set\n                # This is a standard bit manipulation problem to count set bits up to a number\n                # for a specific position.\n                block_size = 1 << i\n                num_full_blocks = (mid + 1) // block_size\n                count_in_full_blocks = num_full_blocks * (block_size // 2)\n                remainder = (mid + 1) % block_size\n                count_in_remainder = max(0, remainder - (block_size // 2))\n                current_sum_of_prices += count_in_full_blocks + count_in_remainder\n\n        if current_sum_of_prices <= k:\n            ans = mid\n            left = mid + 1\n        else:\n            right = mid - 1\n    return ans\n```",
