      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef find_peaks(mountain: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds all the peaks in the given mountain array.\n\n    A peak is defined as an element that is strictly greater than its neighboring elements.\n    The first and last elements of the array are not considered peaks.\n\n    Args:\n        mountain: A 0-indexed array of integers representing the mountain.\n\n    Returns:\n        A list of indices of peaks in the given array in any order.\n    \"\"\"\n    peaks = []\n    n = len(mountain)\n    if n < 3:\n        return peaks\n\n    for i in range(1, n - 1):\n        if mountain[i] > mountain[i - 1] and mountain[i] > mountain[i + 1]:\n            peaks.append(i)\n    return peaks\n```",
