red.\n\nExample 3:\n\nInput: source = \"abcd\", target = \"abce\", original = [\"a\"], changed = [\"e\"], cost = [10000]\nOutput: -1\nExplanation: It is impossible to convert source to target because the value at index 3 cannot be changed from 'd' to 'e'.\n\n \nConstraints:\n\n1 <= source.length == target.length <= 10^5\nsource, target consist of lowercase English letters.\n1 <= cost.length == original.length == changed.length <= 2000\noriginal[i], changed[i] are lowercase English letters.\n1 <= cost[i] <= 10^6\noriginal[i] != changed[i]",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport heapq\n\ndef min_cost_convert(source, target, original, changed, cost):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the minimum cost to convert the string source to the string target.\n\n    Args:\n        source: The initial string.\n        target: The target string.\n        original: A list of characters to be changed.\n        changed: A list of characters to change to.\n        cost: A list of costs corresponding to each change.\n\n    Returns:\n        The minimum cost to convert source to target, or -1 if impossible.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(source)\n    alphabet_size = 26\n    char_to_int = lambda c: ord(c) - ord('a')\n\n    # Initialize distances with infinity\n    dist = [[float('inf')] * alphabet_size for _ in range(alphabet_size)]\n\n    # Set distance from a character to itself to 0\n    for i in range(alphabet_size):\n        dist[i][i] = 0\n\n    # Populate the distance matrix with direct costs\n    for o, c, co in zip(original, changed, cost):\n        u, v = char_to_int(o), char_to_int(c)\n        dist[u][v] = min(dist[u][v], co)\n\n    # Floyd-Warshall algorithm to find all-pairs shortest paths\n    for k in range(alphabet_size):\n        for i in range(alphabet_size):\n            for j in range(alphabet_size):\n                dist[i][j] = min(dist[i][j], dist[i][k] + dist[k][j])\n\n    total_cost = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        source_char_int = char_to_int(source[i])\n        target_char_int = char_to_int(target[i])\n\n        # If source and target characters are the same, no cost\n        if source[i] == target[i]:\n            continue\n\n        # If there's no path from source[i] to target[i], it's impossible\n        if dist[source_char_int][target_char_int] == float('inf'):\n            return -1\n\n        total_cost += dist[source_char_int][target_char_int]\n\n    return total_cost\n```",
