    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef maxFrequencyScore(nums, k):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum possible score by changing elements in the array at most k times.\n    The score is the frequency of the most frequent element in the final array.\n\n    Args:\n        nums: A 0-indexed integer array.\n        k: The maximum number of operations allowed.\n\n    Returns:\n        The maximum score achievable.\n    \"\"\"\n    nums.sort()\n    n = len(nums)\n    prefix_sum = [0] * (n + 1)\n    for i in range(n):\n        prefix_sum[i + 1] = prefix_sum[i] + nums[i]\n\n    max_score = 1\n    left = 0\n    for right in range(n):\n        # Current window: nums[left...right]\n        # We want to make all elements in this window equal to nums[right]\n        # The cost is the sum of absolute differences to nums[right]\n        # cost = sum(nums[right] - nums[i] for i in range(left, right))\n        # cost = (right - left) * nums[right] - sum(nums[i] for i in range(left, right))\n        \n        current_sum = prefix_sum[right] - prefix_sum[left]\n        cost = (right - left) * nums[right] - current_sum\n\n        while cost > k:\n            left += 1\n            current_sum = prefix_sum[right] - prefix_sum[left]\n            cost = (right - left) * nums[right] - current_sum\n        \n        max_score = max(max_score, right - left + 1)\n    \n    return max_score\n\n```",
