      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef is_fascinating(n: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if an integer n is fascinating.\n\n    A number n is fascinating if, after concatenating n with 2 * n and 3 * n,\n    the resulting number contains all digits from 1 to 9 exactly once and no 0s.\n\n    Args:\n        n: An integer consisting of exactly 3 digits.\n\n    Returns:\n        True if n is fascinating, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    concatenated_str = str(n) + str(2 * n) + str(3 * n)\n\n    if '0' in concatenated_str:\n        return False\n\n    if len(concatenated_str) != 9:\n        return False\n\n    digits = sorted(concatenated_str)\n    return digits == ['1', '2', '3', '4', '5', '6', '7', '8', '9']\n```",
