    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef min_partitions(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Given a binary string s, partition the string into one or more substrings\n    such that each substring is beautiful. A string is beautiful if:\n    - It doesn't contain leading zeros.\n    - It's the binary representation of a number that is a power of 5.\n    Return the minimum number of substrings in such partition.\n    If it is impossible to partition the string s into beautiful substrings, return -1.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    powers_of_5 = set()\n    for i in range(16):  # s.length <= 15, so the largest power of 5 could be 5^15\n        powers_of_5.add(str(bin(5**i))[2:])  # Convert to binary and remove '0b' prefix\n\n    n = len(s)\n    dp = [float('inf')] * (n + 1)\n    dp[0] = 0\n\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        for j in range(i):\n            substring = s[j:i]\n            if substring[0] != '0' and substring in powers_of_5:\n                dp[i] = min(dp[i], dp[j] + 1)\n\n    return dp[n] if dp[n] != float('inf') else -1\n```",
