      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef shortest_subarray_with_sum(nums, target):\n    n = len(nums)\n    s = sum(nums)\n\n    # If target is 0, shortest subarray length is 0 (empty subarray)\n    if target == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # Case 1: Target can be achieved within one or two full repetitions of nums\n    # We create a double array to handle subarrays that wrap around the end of nums\n    double_nums = nums + nums\n    prefix_sum_map = {0: -1}  # Map prefix sum to its index\n    current_sum = 0\n    min_len = float('inf')\n\n    for i in range(2 * n):\n        current_sum += double_nums[i]\n        if current_sum - target in prefix_sum_map:\n            min_len = min(min_len, i - prefix_sum_map[current_sum - target])\n        prefix_sum_map[current_sum] = i\n\n    # Case 2: Target requires more than one or two full repetitions of nums\n    if target > s:\n        num_repetitions = target // s\n        remaining_target = target % s\n\n        if remaining_target == 0:\n            # If target is a multiple of s, the shortest subarray is target/s * n\n            # e.g., nums=[1,2,3], s=6, target=12. min_len = 12/6 * 3 = 2*3 = 6\n            min_len = min(min_len, num_repetitions * n)\n        else:\n            # If target is not a multiple of s, we need to find remaining_target\n            # within a single nums array (or within the expanded two-nums array)\n            # and add the length of the full repetitions.\n            temp_prefix_sum_map = {0: -1}\n            temp_current_sum = 0\n            temp_min_len = float('inf')\n            \n            # Search for remaining_target in a single pass of nums\n            for i in range(n):\n                temp_current_sum += nums[i]\n                if temp_current_sum - remaining_target in temp_prefix_sum_map:\n                    temp_min_len = min(temp_min_len, i - temp_prefix_sum_map[temp_current_sum - remaining_target])\n                temp_prefix_sum_map[temp_current_sum] = i\n\n            if temp_min_len != float('inf'):\n                min_len = min(min_len, num_repetitions * n + temp_min_len)\n    \n    # If target is negative (and s is positive), it's impossible to reach.\n    # Similarly, if target is positive and s is negative (unlikely with given constraints nums[i] >= 1),\n    # but the logic covers it by finding if a suitable subarray exists.\n    # Given constraints 1 <= nums[i], s will always be positive. If target < 0, it's impossible.\n    # The problem constraints state 1 <= target, so target is always positive.\n\n    return min_len if min_len != float('inf') else -1\n\n```",
