    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef find_error_nums(grid):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the repeating and missing numbers in a grid.\n\n    Args:\n        grid: A 0-indexed 2D integer matrix of size n * n.\n\n    Returns:\n        A 0-indexed integer array ans of size 2 where ans[0] equals to the\n        repeating number and ans[1] equals to the missing number.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(grid)\n    seen = set()\n    repeating = -1\n    total_sum = 0\n\n    for row in grid:\n        for num in row:\n            if num in seen:\n                repeating = num\n            seen.add(num)\n            total_sum += num\n\n    # The sum of numbers from 1 to n*n is n*(n+1)//2.\n    # The sum of numbers in the grid is total_sum.\n    # The difference between the actual sum and the expected sum is\n    # (repeating + missing) - (sum of unique numbers in grid).\n    # Since we have the repeating number, we can find the missing number.\n\n    expected_sum = n * (n * n + 1) // 2\n    missing = expected_sum - (total_sum - repeating)\n\n    return [repeating, missing]\n```",
