er indices, the set of values will not be {a, ..., a+K-1}.\n                    # For example, if we have {a, a+1, ..., a+K-1} at indices `idx1 < idx2 < ... < idxK`,\n                    # and we also pick an index `j` where `P[j]` is NOT in `{a, ..., a+K-1}`,\n                    # then the set of values at the chosen indices would include `P[j]`, violating the condition.\n                    # Similarly, if we don't pick an index for one of `a, ..., a+K-1`, that value is missing.\n                    # Therefore, the set of indices `{i_1, ..., i_K}` must be exactly the set\n                    # `{pos[a], pos[a+1], ..., pos[a+K-1]}`.\n\n                    sorted_indices = sorted(indices_of_a_to_a_plus_K_minus_1)\n                    i_1 = sorted_indices[0]\n                    i_K = sorted_indices[-1]\n                    min_diff = min(min_diff, i_K - i_1)\n\n    print(min_diff)\n\n\ndef solve_optimized():\n    N, K = map(int, sys.stdin.readline().split())\n    P = list(map(int, sys.stdin.readline().split()))\n\n    min_diff = float('inf')\n\n    # Precompute the position of each value.\n    # `pos[v]` will store the 0-based index of the value `v` in `P`.\n    pos = [0] * (N + 1)\n    for i in range(N):\n        pos[P[i]] = i\n\n    # We iterate through all possible contiguous sequences of K integers.\n    # A sequence is defined by its starting number `a`, where `1 <= a <= N - K + 1`.\n    # The sequence of values is `a, a+1, ..., a+K-1`.\n    # For the subsequence `P_{i_1}, ..., P_{i_K}` to be a rearrangement of `a, ..., a+K-1`,\n    # the set of values `{P_{i_1}, ..., P_{i_K}}` must be exactly `{a, ..., a+K-1}\\}$.\n    # This implies that the indices `i_1, ..., i_K` must be exactly the indices where the values `a, ..., a+K-1` appear in `P`.\n    # Let these indices be `idx_a, idx_{a+1}, ..., idx_{a+K-1}` (0-based).\n    # Then the required `i_1, ..., i_K` (1-based) will be the sorted list of `idx_a + 1, ..., idx_{a+K-1} + 1`.\n    # We want to minimize `i_K 