e, we return 6.\n\nExample 3:\n\nInput: nums = [1]\nOutput: 1\nExplanation:\nThere is a single subarray of nums which is [1], with its largest element 1. The first element is 1 and the last element is also 1.\nHence, we return 1.\n\n \nConstraints:\n\n1 <= nums.length <= 10^5\n1 <= nums[i] <= 10^9",
