    "prompt": "Generate an executable Python function generated from the given prompt. Return the function body without invoking it at the final solution. Question:\nYou are given a string s and an integer k.\nDefine a function distance(s_1, s_2) between two strings s_1 and s_2 of the same length n as:\n\nThe sum of the minimum distance between s_1[i] and s_2[i] when the characters from 'a' to 'z' are placed in a cyclic order, for all i in the range [0, n - 1].\n\nFor example, distance(\"ab\", \"cd\") == 4, and distance(\"a\", \"z\") == 1.\nYou can change any letter of s to any other lowercase English letter, any number of times.\nReturn a string denoting the lexicographically smallest string t you can get after some changes, such that distance(s, t) <= k.\n \nExample 1:\n\nInput: s = \"zbbz\", k = 3\nOutput: \"aaaz\"\nExplanation:\nChange s to \"aaaz\". The distance between \"zbbz\" and \"aaaz\" is equal to k = 3.\n\nExample 2:\n\nInput: s = \"xaxcd\", k = 4\nOutput: \"aawcd\"\nExplanation:\nThe distance between \"xaxcd\" and \"aawcd\" is equal to k = 4.\n\nExample 3:\n\nInput: s = \"lol\", k = 0\nOutput: \"lol\"\nExplanation:\nIt's impossible to change any character as k = 0.\n\n \nConstraints:\n\n1 <= s.length <= 100\n0 <= k <= 2000\ns consists only of lowercase English letters.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve(s: str, k: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the lexicographically smallest string t such that the distance(s, t) <= k.\n\n    Args:\n        s: The input string.\n        k: The maximum allowed distance.\n\n    Returns:\n        The lexicographically smallest string t.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(s)\n    t_list = list(s)\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        # Calculate distance to 'a'\n        dist_to_a = ord(s[i]) - ord('a')\n        # Calculate distance to 'z' (cyclic)\n        dist_to_z = ord('z') - ord(s[i]) + 1\n\n        min_dist_to_endpoints = min(dist_to_a, dist_to_z)\n\n        if min_dist_to_endpoints <= k:\n            if dist_to_a <= dist_to_z:\n                # Prefer changing to 'a' if it's closer or equal distance and 'a' is lexicographically smaller\n                change_amount = dist_to_a\n                t_list[i] = 'a'\n            else:\n                # Change to 'z' if it's closer and lexicographically within the cyclic distance\n                change_amount = dist_to_z\n                # We don't explicitly change to 'z' here because we want the lexicographically smallest.\n                # If 'a' is not closer and we can afford to change, we aim for 'a' first.\n                # The logic below handles changes to characters other than 'a'.\n                pass # This case will be handled by the general character change logic\n\n            k -= change_amount\n        else:\n            # If neither 'a' nor 'z' is reachable within k, try to change to a character closer to 'a' as much as possible.\n            # We prioritize moving towards 'a' lexicographically.\n            target_char_ord = ord(s[i]) - min(k, dist_to_a)\n            t_list[i] = chr(target_char_ord)\n            k -= (ord(s[i]) - target_char_ord)\n\n    return \"\".join(t_list)\n```",
