      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef matrix_score(nums):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the final score by repeatedly selecting the largest number from each row,\n    removing it, and adding the maximum of the removed numbers to the score.\n\n    Args:\n        nums: A 0-indexed 2D integer array.\n\n    Returns:\n        The final score.\n    \"\"\"\n    score = 0\n    num_rows = len(nums)\n    if not num_rows:\n        return 0\n\n    num_cols = len(nums[0])\n    if not num_cols:\n        return 0\n\n    # Sort each row in descending order\n    for i in range(num_rows):\n        nums[i].sort(reverse=True)\n\n    # Iterate through the columns (which now represent the order of removal after sorting)\n    for j in range(num_cols):\n        max_removed_in_round = 0\n        for i in range(num_rows):\n            # The largest remaining number in each row is at the current column index\n            max_removed_in_round = max(max_removed_in_round, nums[i][j])\n        score += max_removed_in_round\n\n    return score\n```",
