      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport heapq\n\ndef max_groups_of_distinct_numbers(usageLimits: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum number of groups that can be created satisfying the given conditions.\n\n    Args:\n        usageLimits: A 0-indexed array where usageLimits[i] is the maximum number of times\n                     number i can be used across all groups.\n\n    Returns:\n        An integer representing the maximum number of groups.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(usageLimits)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # Max-heap to store the available counts of each number.\n    # We use a max-heap because we want to prioritize using numbers that have more remaining uses\n    # when fulfilling group requirements.\n    available_counts = []\n    for i in range(n):\n        if usageLimits[i] > 0:\n            heapq.heappush(available_counts, -usageLimits[i])  # Store as negative for max-heap behavior\n\n    groups = 0\n    current_group_length = 0\n\n    while available_counts:\n        temp_items = []\n        count_for_current_group = current_group_length + 1\n        items_popped = 0\n\n        # Try to form a new group with length `count_for_current_group`\n        while available_counts and items_popped < count_for_current_group:\n            item_count = -heapq.heappop(available_counts)  # Get actual count\n\n            if item_count > 0:\n                temp_items.append(-(item_count - 1))  # Reduce count and store for re-adding\n                items_popped += 1\n            else:\n                # This should ideally not happen if we only add positive counts\n                pass\n\n        if items_popped == count_for_current_group:\n            groups += 1\n            current_group_length = count_for_current_group\n            # Re-add items that were used and still have remaining counts\n            for item in temp_items:\n                if item < 0:  # If count is still positive after decrementing\n                   