    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef minCost(s1: str, s2: str, x: int) -> int:\n    n = len(s1)\n    diff_indices = [i for i in range(n) if s1[i] != s2[i]]\n\n    if len(diff_indices) % 2 != 0:\n        return -1\n\n    if not diff_indices:\n        return 0\n\n    # dp[i][j] will store the minimum cost to resolve the first i differing indices\n    # where j represents the number of pairs of adjacent flips used.\n    # Maximum possible adjacent flips is n // 2.\n    dp = [[float('inf')] * (n // 2 + 1) for _ in range(len(diff_indices) + 1)]\n\n    # Base case: 0 differing indices, 0 adjacent flips cost 0\n    dp[0][0] = 0\n\n    for i in range(1, len(diff_indices) + 1):\n        for j in range(n // 2 + 1):\n            # Option 1: Use a global flip (cost x) to resolve the current differing index\n            # This requires either 0 adjacent flips for this step or resolves a pair.\n            # If we use a global flip for the i-th differing index, it means we are pairing it\n            # with some previous differing index.\n            # The cost to reach this state from the previous state where we considered (i-1) differing\n            # indices and used j adjacent flips.\n            dp[i][j] = min(dp[i][j], dp[i-1][j] + x)\n\n            # Option 2: Use adjacent flips\n            # If the current differing index and the previous differing index are adjacent\n            if diff_indices[i-1] == diff_indices[i-2] + 1:\n                # We can use an adjacent flip to resolve both diff_indices[i-2] and diff_indices[i-1]\n                # This means the cost comes from the state where we considered (i-2) differing indices\n                # and used (j-1) adjacent flips.\n                if j > 0:\n                    dp[i][j] = min(dp[i][j], dp[i-2][j-1] + 1)\n\n    # The minimum cost is the minimum value in the last row of dp,\n    # considering all possible numbers of adjacent flips.\n    min_total_cost = float('inf')\n    for j in range(n // 2 + 1):\n        min_total_cost = min(min_total_cost, dp[len(diff_indices)][j])\n\n    return min_total_cost if min_total_cost != float('inf') else -1\n\n```",
