      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef sumIndicesWithKSetBits(nums: list[int], k: int) -> int:\n    total_sum = 0\n    for i in range(len(nums)):\n        # Count set bits in the binary representation of the index i\n        set_bits_count = 0\n        num = i\n        while num > 0:\n            num &= (num - 1)  # Brian Kernighan's algorithm to count set bits\n            set_bits_count += 1\n\n        # If the number of set bits is equal to k, add the corresponding element to the sum\n        if set_bits_count == k:\n            total_sum += nums[i]\n    return total_sum\n```",
