      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef get_maximum_good_subarray_sum(nums, k):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum sum of a \"good\" subarray.\n\n    A subarray nums[i..j] is good if |nums[i] - nums[j]| == k.\n\n    Args:\n        nums: A list of integers.\n        k: A positive integer.\n\n    Returns:\n        The maximum sum of a good subarray. If there are no good subarrays, returns 0.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(nums)\n    max_sum = float('-inf')\n    found_good_subarray = False\n\n    # Calculate prefix sums to efficiently compute subarray sums\n    prefix_sum = [0] * (n + 1)\n    for i in range(n):\n        prefix_sum[i + 1] = prefix_sum[i] + nums[i]\n\n    # Iterate through all possible ending indices j\n    for j in range(n):\n        # Iterate through all possible starting indices i\n        for i in range(j + 1):\n            if abs(nums[i] - nums[j]) == k:\n                current_sum = prefix_sum[j + 1] - prefix_sum[i]\n                max_sum = max(max_sum, current_sum)\n                found_good_subarray = True\n\n    if found_good_subarray:\n        return max_sum\n    else:\n        return 0\n```",
