      "generated_answer": "Let's analyze each statement:\n\nStatement 1: \"As of 2020, some models attain greater than 98% accuracy on CIFAR-10.\"\nBy 2020, state-of-the-art models, often leveraging advanced architectures and training techniques, had indeed surpassed 98% accuracy on CIFAR-10. Many deep learning models achieved accuracies in the high 90s.\n\nStatement 2: \"The original ResNets were not optimized with the Adam optimizer.\"\nThe original ResNet paper (He et al., 2015) indeed primarily used stochastic gradient descent (SGD) with momentum for optimization, not Adam. While ResNets can be trained with Adam, it wasn't the optimizer used in their initial breakthrough publication. Adam became more prevalent later.\n\nBased on this analysis:\nStatement 1 is true.\nStatement 2 is true.\n\nTherefore, the most likely correct answer is \"True, True\".\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{G}$.",
