      "generated_answer": "The Central Processing Unit (CPU) is primarily composed of the Control Unit (CU) and the Arithmetic Logic Unit (ALU). The CU manages the flow of data and instructions, while the ALU performs arithmetic and logical operations. While cache memory and registers are crucial for CPU performance, they are often considered components rather than entirely separate functional units in basic breakdowns.\n\nThe most accurate and commonly accepted answer describing the *major* functional units of a CPU is the Control Unit and the Arithmetic Logic Unit. Therefore, option B, which lists these two as the major functional units, is the most appropriate.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{B}$.",
