    "global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9272",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Statement 1| The BLEU metric uses precision, while the ROGUE metric uses recall. Statement 2| Hidden markov models were frequently used to model English sentences.\n\nOptions: \nA. Mostly True, Mostly False\nB. Mostly False, Mostly True\nC. False, True\nD. False, Cannot be determined\nE. Cannot be determined, False\nF. True, True\nG. Cannot be determined, True\nH. False, False\nI. True, Cannot be determined\nJ. True, False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Statement 1 is mostly true. BLEU primarily focuses on precision by measuring the overlap of n-grams between the candidate and reference translations. ROGUE, on the other hand, heavily relies on recall by measuring how many n-grams from the reference summaries are present in the candidate.\n\nStatement 2 is mostly false. While Hidden Markov Models (HMMs) were used for language modeling in early NLP, Recurrent Neural Networks (RNNs) and their variants like LSTMs and GRUs became more prevalent for modeling English sentences due to their ability to capture sequential dependencies better.\n\nTherefore, the most likely correct answer is A. Mostly True, Mostly False.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{A}$.",
