      "generated_answer": "The provided text explains currying as the process of reducing a function with multiple arguments to a function with fewer arguments. The example shows how `real x real -> real` can be transformed into `real -> (real -> real)`. This implies we're reducing a multi-argument function into a series of single-argument functions. Therefore, currying can be applied to any function to break down its multiple arguments into a sequence of single arguments.\n\nThe correct answer is $\\boxed{A}$.",
