    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let's analyze each statement.\n\nStatement 1: \"L2 regularization of linear models tends to make models more sparse than L1 regularization.\"\nL1 regularization (Lasso) encourages sparsity by driving some coefficients exactly to zero. L2 regularization (Ridge) shrinks coefficients towards zero but rarely makes them exactly zero, thus producing less sparse models. Therefore, this statement is False.\n\nStatement 2: \"Residual connections can be found in ResNets and Transformers.\"\nResNets are explicitly known for their residual blocks, which use residual connections. Transformers also heavily utilize residual connections within their encoder and decoder blocks, often around the multi-head attention and feed-forward layers. Therefore, this statement is True.\n\nBased on the analysis, Statement 1 is False and Statement 2 is True. This corresponds to the option \"False, True\".\n\nThe correct answer is \\boxed{B}.",
