    "global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9108",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Suppose we have the following objective function: $\\argmin_{{w}} \\frac{{1}}{{2}} \\norm{{Xw-y}}^2_2 + \\frac{{1}}{{2}}\\gamma \\norm{{w}}^2_2$ What is the gradient of $\\frac{{1}}{{2}} \\norm{{Xw-y}}^2_2 + \\frac{{1}}{{2}}\\lambda \\norm{{w}}^2_2$ with respect to $w$?\n\nOptions: \nA. $\\nabla_w f(w) = X^\\top X w - X^\\top y + \\lambda w$\nB. $\\nabla_w f(w) = X^\\top X w - X^\\top y + \\lambda I$\nC. $\\nabla_w f(w) = X^\\top X w - X^\\top y + (\\lambda+1) w$\nD. $\\nabla_w f(w) = X^\\top X w - X^\\top y + \\lambda$\nE. $\\nabla_w f(w) = X^\\top X w + X^\\top y + \\lambda w$\nF. $\\nabla_w f(w) = X^\\top X w - X^\\top y - \\lambda w$\nG. $\\nabla_w f(w) = (X^\\top X + \\lambda I)w - X^\\top y + \\lambda w$\nH. $\\nabla_w f(w) = X^\\top X + \\lambda I)w - X^\\top y$\nI. $\\nabla_w f(w) = X^\\top X w - X^\\top y + \\lambda^2 w$\nJ. $\\nabla_w f(w) = X^\\top X w + X^\\top y - \\lambda w$\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The objective function is $f(w) = \\frac{1}{2} \\norm{Xw-y}^2_2 + \\frac{1}{2}\\lambda \\norm{w}^2_2$.\nLet's compute the gradient of each term separately.\n\nThe gradient of the first term $\\frac{1}{2} \\norm{Xw-y}^2_2$ with respect to $w$ is:\n$\\nabla_w \\left( \\frac{1}{2} \\norm{Xw-y}^2_2 \\right) = \\nabla_w \\left( \\frac{1}{2} (Xw-y)^\\top (Xw-y) \\right)$\n$= \\nabla_w \\left( \\frac{1}{2} (w^\\top X^\\top - y^\\top) (Xw-y) \\right)$\n$= \\nabla_w \\left( \\frac{1}{2} (w^\\top X^\\top X w - w^\\top X^\\top y - y^\\top X w + y^\\top y) \\right)$\nSince $y^\\top X w = (y^\\top X w)^\\top = w^\\top X^\\top y$, we have:\n$= \\nabla_w \\left( \\frac{1}{2} (w^\\top X^\\top X w - 2w^\\top X^\\top y + y^\\top y) \\right)$\nUsing the matrix calculus rule $\\nabla_w (w^\\top A w) = (A+A^\\top)w$ and $\\nabla_w (w^\\top b) = b$, and assuming $X^\\top X$ is symmetric:\n$= \\frac{1}{2} (2 X^\\top X w - 2 X^\\top y) = X^\\top X w - X^\\top y$\n\nThe gradient of the second term $\\frac{1}{2}\\lambda \\norm{w}^2_2$ with respect to $w$ is:\n$\\nabla_w \\left( \\frac{1}{2}\\lambda \\norm{w}^2_2 \\right) = \\nabla_w \\left( \\frac{1}{2}\\lambda w^\\top w \\right)$\nUsing the matrix calculus rule $\\nabla_w (w^\\top w) = 2w$:\n$= \\frac{1}{2}\\lambda (2w) = \\lambda w$\n\nCombining the gradients of both terms:\n$\\nabla_w f(w) = (X^\\top X w - X^\\top y) + \\lambda w$\n$\\nabla_w f(w) = X^\\top X w - X^\\top y + \\lambda w$\n\nComparing this with the given options, option A matches our result.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{A}$.",
