    "global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9114",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Given 2 colors whose HSI representations are given as follows: (a) $(pi, 0.3,0.5)$, (b) $(0.5 pi, 0.8,0.3)$, which color is brighter?\n\nOptions: \nA. Brightness cannot be compared without additional information about the viewing conditions\nB. (b) is brighter due to higher hue value\nC. Cannot be determined from the given data\nD. Brightness is subjective and cannot be determined from HSI values alone\nE. (b) is brighter because it has a higher saturation and lower hue value\nF. (a)\nG. Both are equally bright\nH. (b)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
