    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How many labeled trees are there on 6 vertices?\n\nOptions: \nA. 2500\nB. 3000\nC. 864\nD. 1800\nE. 720\nF. 2000\nG. 1500\nH. 1000\nI. 1296\nJ. 500\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The number of labeled trees on n vertices is given by Cayley's formula, which states that there are $n^{n-2}$ such trees. For n=6 vertices, the number of labeled trees is $6^{6-2} = 6^4$.\nCalculating $6^4$:\n$6^4 = 6 \\times 6 \\times 6 \\times 6 = 36 \\times 36$.\n$36 \\times 36 = 1296$.\n\nTherefore, there are 1296 labeled trees on 6 vertices.\n\nComparing this result with the given options:\nA. 2500\nB. 3000\nC. 864\nD. 1800\nE. 720\nF. 2000\nG. 1500\nH. 1000\nI. 1296\nJ. 500\n\nThe calculated number matches option I.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{I}$.",
