  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9148",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A remote database contains 30 seconds of color motion-video. The video sequence is of the format (352 ́288 pixels) with RGB digitization at 30 frames per second. Find the the data rate for this motion-video in Mbits/s (3 sig. fig.).\n\nOptions: \nA. 69.6\nB. 64.3\nC. 45.6\nD. 91.2\nE. 60.8\nF. 78.4\nG. 56.2\nH. 82.5\nI. 73.1\nJ. 85.3\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To calculate the data rate, we first need to find the total number of bits per frame.\nNumber of pixels per frame = width × height = 352 × 288 pixels.\nSince it is RGB digitization, each pixel requires 3 bytes (1 byte for Red, 1 for Green, 1 for Blue).\nNumber of bits per frame = (352 × 288 pixels) × (3 bytes/pixel) × (8 bits/byte).\nNumber of bits per frame = 352 × 288 × 3 × 8 bits.\nNumber of bits per frame = 2,427,392 bits.\n\nThe video is at 30 frames per second, so the data rate in bits per second is:\nData rate (bits/s) = (Number of bits per frame) × (frames per second)\nData rate (bits/s) = 2,427,392 bits/frame × 30 frames/s\nData rate (bits/s) = 72,821,760 bits/s.\n\nTo convert this to Mbits/s, we divide by 1,000,000:\nData rate (Mbits/s) = 72,821,760 / 1,000,000 Mbits/s\nData rate (Mbits/s) = 72.82176 Mbits/s.\n\nRounding to 3 significant figures, the data rate is 72.8 Mbits/s.\n\nLet's recheck the calculation:\nNumber of pixels per frame = 352 * 288 = 101376 pixels\nBits per pixel = 3 bytes/pixel * 8 bits/byte = 24 bits/pixel\nBits per frame = 101376 pixels * 24 bits/pixel = 2433024 bits/frame\nData rate = 2433024 bits/frame * 30 frames/second = 72990720 bits/second\nData rate in Mbits/s = 72990720 / 1000000 = 72.99072 Mbits/s\nRounding to 3 significant figures gives 73.0 Mbits/s.\n\nLooking at the options again:\nA. 69.6\nB. 64.3\nC. 45.6\nD. 91.2\nE. 60.8\nF. 78.4\nG. 56.2\nH. 82.5\nI. 73.1\nJ. 85.3\n\nThe closest option is I. 73.1. It's possible there's a slight difference in how \"Mbits\" is interpreted (e.g., using 1024 instead of 1000 for conversion, although usually for data rates 1000 is used). If we use 1024 for Kbits and 1024*1024 for Mbits, it won't change the result significantly for this magnitude. Let's assume the calculation is correct and 73.1 is the closest option due to rounding or slight variations in the problem statement or options.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{I}$.",
