    "global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9149",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Suppose Host A wants to send a large file to Host B. The path from Host A to Host B has three links, of rates R1 = 500 kbps, R2 = 2 Mbps, and R3 = Mbps. Suppose the file is 4 million bytes. Dividing the file size by the throughput, roughly how many seconds will it take to transfer the file to Host B?\n\nOptions: \nA. 70\nB. 40\nC. 90\nD. 120\nE. 100\nF. 64\nG. 50\nH. 30\nI. 110\nJ. 80\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The bottleneck link will determine the overall transfer rate. In this case, R1 = 500 kbps is the slowest link, so the throughput is 500 kbps.\nThe file size is 4 million bytes, which is 4 * 1024 * 1024 * 8 bits.\nTime = File Size / Throughput = (4 * 1024 * 1024 * 8 bits) / (500 * 1000 bits/sec) ≈ 67.1 seconds.\nThe closest option is 70 seconds.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{A}$.",
