  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9219",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the output of the following program? PROGRAM TEST (output); VAR I, J, K, COUNT : integer; BEGIN I: = 1; J: = 2; K: = 3; count: = 1; write1n (I div J, K mod J); while count < = 3 DO BEGIN If I < J then If K > J then If (K > I) or (I = J) then write1n (I) ELSE write1n (J) ELSE write1n (K); CASE COUNT OF 1: J: = 0; 2: BEGIN K: = K - 1; J: = J + K END; 3:I: = 2 \\textasteriskcentered I; END; count : = count + 1; END {{while count........}} END.\n\nOptions: \nA. 2 2\nB. 2 3\nC. 1 0\nD. 0 2\nE. 3 2\nF. 0 1\nG. 2 1\nH. 3 0\nI. 1 1\nJ. 1 2\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
