    "global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9235",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: At time 0, five jobs are available for execution on a single processor, with service times of 25, 15, 5, 3, and 2 time units. Which of the following is the minimum value of the average completion time of these jobs?\n\nOptions: \nA. 40\nB. 10\nC. 76/5\nD. 100/5\nE. 60\nF. 208/5\nG. 92/5\nH. 30\nI. 20\nJ. 50\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The minimum average completion time for jobs on a single processor is achieved by executing them in the order of their service times, from shortest to longest (Shortest Job First scheduling). The service times are 2, 3, 5, 15, and 25.\n\nThe completion times are:\nJob 1 (service time 2): 2\nJob 2 (service time 3): 2 + 3 = 5\nJob 3 (service time 5): 5 + 5 = 10\nJob 4 (service time 15): 10 + 15 = 25\nJob 5 (service time 25): 25 + 25 = 50\n\nThe total completion time is 2 + 5 + 10 + 25 + 50 = 92.\nThe average completion time is the total completion time divided by the number of jobs: 92 / 5.\n\nComparing this to the given options:\nA. 40\nB. 10\nC. 76/5 = 15.2\nD. 100/5 = 20\nE. 60\nF. 208/5 = 41.6\nG. 92/5 = 18.4\nH. 30\nI. 20\nJ. 50\n\nThe calculated average completion time is 92/5. However, the provided options do not exactly match the calculated value and there might be a slight discrepancy in the options or the question's intended calculation. Let's re-examine the question and options, assuming there might be a misunderstanding or typo.\n\nLet's re-calculate the completion times and average completion time carefully.\nService times: 2, 3, 5, 15, 25.\nOrder of execution (shortest first): 2, 3, 5, 15, 25.\n\nCompletion times:\nJob 1 (2): 2\nJob 2 (3): 2 + 3 = 5\nJob 3 (5): 5 + 5 = 10\nJob 4 (15): 10 + 15 = 25\nJob 5 (25): 25 + 25 = 50\n\nTotal completion time = 2 + 5 + 10 + 25 + 50 = 92.\nAverage completion time = 92 / 5 = 18.4.\n\nNow let's compare again with the options.\nOption G is 92/5.\n\nFinal Answer is G.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{G}$.",
