    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The Bayesian network H -> U <- P <- W has four variables: H, U, P, and W.\nWe need to determine the number of independent parameters for each conditional probability distribution.\n- P(H) requires 2-1 = 1 parameter (if binary).\n- P(W) requires 2-1 = 1 parameter (if binary).\n- P(U | H, P) requires 2 * 2 * (2-1) = 4 parameters (if binary).\n- P(P | W) requires 2 * (2-1) = 2 parameters (if binary).\nThe total number of independent parameters is the sum of parameters for each conditional probability distribution: 1 + 1 + 4 + 2 = 8.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{D}$.",
