    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Consider Convolutional Neural Network D2 which takes input images of size 32x32 with 1 colour channels. The first layer of D2 uses 4 filters of size 5x5, a stride of 2, and zero-padding of width 1. The dimensions of the resulting activation map for each filter in this first layer will be k x k. What is the value of k?\n\nOptions: \nA. 25\nB. 14\nC. 20\nD. 15\nE. 16\nF. 28\nG. 22\nH. 24\nI. 30\nJ. 18\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The formula for calculating the dimensions of the output activation map in a convolutional layer is:\n$k = \\lfloor \\frac{(W - F + 2P)}{S} \\rfloor + 1$\nwhere:\n$W$ is the input width (or height).\n$F$ is the filter size.\n$P$ is the padding.\n$S$ is the stride.\n\nIn this case, $W = 32$, $F = 5$, $P = 1$, and $S = 2$.\nPlugging these values into the formula:\n$k = \\lfloor \\frac{(32 - 5 + 2 \\times 1)}{2} \\rfloor + 1$\n$k = \\lfloor \\frac{(32 - 5 + 2)}{2} \\rfloor + 1$\n$k = \\lfloor \\frac{29}{2} \\rfloor + 1$\n$k = \\lfloor 14.5 \\rfloor + 1$\n$k = 14 + 1$\n$k = 15$\n\nThe dimensions of the resulting activation map for each filter will be 15x15.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{D}$.",
