      "generated_answer": "Let $L$ be the number of leaves and $I$ be the number of nonterminal nodes in a complete K-ary tree of depth $N$.\nThe total number of nodes in a complete K-ary tree of depth $N$ is $T = \\sum_{i=0}^{N} K^i$.\nThe number of nonterminal nodes are the nodes at depths $0$ to $N-1$. So, $I = \\sum_{i=0}^{N-1} K^i = \\frac{K^N - 1}{K-1}$.\nThe number of leaves are the nodes at depth $N$. So, $L = K^N$.\nThe total number of nodes is $T = I + L = \\frac{K^N - 1}{K-1} + K^N = \\frac{K^N - 1 + K^{N+1} - K^N}{K-1} = \\frac{K^{N+1} - 1}{K-1}$.\n\nWe want to find the ratio of the number of nonterminal nodes to the total number of nodes, which is $\\frac{I}{T}$.\n$\\frac{I}{T} = \\frac{\\frac{K^N - 1}{K-1}}{\\frac{K^{N+1} - 1}{K-1}} = \\frac{K^N - 1}{K^{N+1} - 1}$.\n\nFor large $N$, $K^N - 1 \\approx K^N$ and $K^{N+1} - 1 \\approx K^{N+1}$.\nSo, $\\frac{I}{T} \\approx \\frac{K^N}{K^{N+1}} = \\frac{1}{K}$.\n\nLet's look at the options.\nWe are looking for the ratio of nonterminal nodes to the total number of nodes.\nFor large N, the number of leaves ($K^N$) is much larger than the number of nonterminal nodes ($\\frac{K^N-1}{K-1}$).\nThe ratio of nonterminal nodes to total nodes will be close to the ratio of nonterminal nodes to leaves.\n\nLet's re-examine the total number of nodes:\nAt depth 0, there is 1 node.\nAt depth 1, there are K nodes.\nAt depth 2, there are $K^2$ nodes.\n...\nAt depth N, there are $K^N$ nodes.\nTotal number of nodes, $T = 1 + K + K^2 + ... + K^N = \\frac{K^{N+1}-1}{K-1}$.\n\nNumber of nonterminal nodes are nodes at depths $0, 1, ..., N-1$.\nNumber of nonterminal nodes, $I = 1 + K + K^2 + ... + K^{N-1} = \\frac{K^N-1}{K-1}$.\n\nRatio of nonterminal nodes to total nodes = $\\frac{I}{T} = \\frac{\\frac{K^N-1}{K-1}}{\\frac{K^{N+1}-1}{K-1}} = \\frac{K^N-1}{K^{N+1}-1}$.\n\nFor large $N$, $K^N-1 \\approx K^N$ and $K^{N+1}-1 \\approx K^{N+1}$.\nSo, $\\frac{I}{T} \\approx \\frac{K^N}{K^{N+1}} = \\frac{1}{K}$.\n\nThus, of the given options, $1/K$ best approximates the ratio of the number of nonterminal nodes to the total number of nodes in a complete K-ary tree of depth N.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{J}$.",
