    "global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9308",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Say the incidence of a disease D is about 5 cases per 100 people (i.e., P(D) = 0.05). Let Boolean random variable D mean a patient “has disease D” and let Boolean random variable TP stand for \"tests positive.\" Tests for disease D are known to be very accurate in the sense that the probability of testing positive when you have the disease is 0.99, and the probability of testing negative when you do not have the disease is 0.97. What is P(TP), the prior probability of testing positive.\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.051\nB. 0.091\nC. 0.0368\nD. 0.025\nE. None of the above\nF. 0.473\nG. All of the above\nH. 0.099\nI. 0.078\nJ. 0.065\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let D be the event that a patient has the disease D, and TP be the event that the patient tests positive.\nWe are given:\nP(D) = 0.05 (incidence of the disease)\nP(TP | D) = 0.99 (probability of testing positive given the disease, also known as sensitivity)\nP(¬TP | ¬D) = 0.97 (probability of testing negative given no disease, also known as specificity)\n\nFrom the given information, we can deduce:\nP(¬D) = 1 - P(D) = 1 - 0.05 = 0.95 (probability of not having the disease)\nP(TP | ¬D) = 1 - P(¬TP | ¬D) = 1 - 0.97 = 0.03 (probability of testing positive given no disease, also known as the false positive rate)\n\nWe want to find P(TP), the prior probability of testing positive. We can use the law of total probability:\nP(TP) = P(TP | D) * P(D) + P(TP | ¬D) * P(¬D)\n\nSubstitute the known values into the formula:\nP(TP) = (0.99 * 0.05) + (0.03 * 0.95)\nP(TP) = 0.0495 + 0.0285\nP(TP) = 0.078\n\nNow, let's compare this result with the given options:\nA. 0.051\nB. 0.091\nC. 0.0368\nD. 0.025\nE. None of the above\nF. 0.473\nG. All of the above\nH. 0.099\nI. 0.078\nJ. 0.065\n\nOur calculated value of P(TP) is 0.078, which matches option I.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{I}$.",
      "success": true,
