    "global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9406",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Given a color image of size 28 x 28 x 3 pixels, how many convolutional filters in the first layer of a Convolutional Neural Network if the first layer's output tensor has size 26 x 26 x 64?\n\nOptions: \nA. 96\nB. 512\nC. 1024\nD. 64\nE. 48\nF. 72\nG. 256\nH. 32\nI. 128\nJ. 192\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The output tensor size of a convolutional layer is determined by the input size, kernel size, padding, stride, and the number of filters. Given the input image size is 28 x 28 x 3 and the output feature map size is 26 x 26 x 64, we can deduce information about the convolutional operation. The reduction in spatial dimensions from 28x28 to 26x26 suggests a kernel size of 3x3 with a stride of 1 and no padding (or a specific combination of padding and stride that results in this reduction). The third dimension of the output tensor (64) directly corresponds to the number of convolutional filters used in that layer. Each filter generates one feature map at the output. Therefore, if the output tensor has a depth of 64, it means 64 convolutional filters were applied.\n\nThe correct answer is \\boxed{D}.",
