    "global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9410",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Let a undirected graph G with edges E = {{<0,2>,<1,4>,<9,6>,<8,12>,<2,4>,<1,3>,<1,5>,<12,1>,<8,1>,<5,9>,<0,10>,<5,2>,<0,8>,<3,4>,<3,11>,<7,1>,<2,1>,<0,12>,<1,0>,<7,8>}}, which <A,B> represent Node A is connected to Node B. What is the minimum vertex cover of G? Represent the vertex cover in a list of ascending order.\n\nOptions: \nA. [0, 2, 3, 4, 7, 8, 10]\nB. [0, 1, 3, 4, 5, 8, 12]\nC. [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 7, 8, 9]\nD. [0, 1, 2, 4, 7, 9]\nE. [0, 2, 3, 5, 8, 11]\nF. [1, 3, 4, 5, 8, 10]\nG. [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 8]\nH. [0, 1, 2, 3, 5, 6, 8, 9]\nI. [0, 1, 2, 3, 8, 9]\nJ. [1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 8, 9, 12]\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
