    "global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9437",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Consider the Bayesian network given below. How many independent parameters would we need if we made no assumptions about independence or conditional independence H -> U <- P <- W?\n\nOptions: \nA. 8\nB. 15\nC. 10\nD. 3\nE. 12\nF. 7\nG. 25\nH. 4\nI. 5\nJ. 20\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "openai/gpt-4o-mini",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To determine the number of independent parameters needed for the Bayesian network H -> U <- P <- W, we can consider the structure and the number of conditional probability tables (CPTs) associated with each node. In a network with N nodes, assuming no independence or conditional independence, we typically need parameters equal to the number of configurations of each parent node. In this case, the most reasonable count gives us 8 independent parameters considering the different combinations for the parent nodes and the relationships in the network.\n\nThus, the correct answer is \\boxed{A}.",
