    "global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9442",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: We are training fully connected network with two hidden layers to predict housing prices. Inputs are $100$-dimensional, and have several features such as the number of square feet, the median family income, etc. The first hidden layer has $1000$ activations. The second hidden layer has $10$ activations. The output is a scalar representing the house price. Assuming a vanilla network with affine transformations and with no batch normalization and no learnable parameters in the activation function, how many parameters does this network have?\n\nOptions: \nA. 120010\nB. 111110\nC. 100121\nD. 112110\nE. 110010\nF. 110020\nG. 122121\nH. 110011\nI. 111021\nJ. 130021\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let the input dimension be $D_{in} = 100$.\nThe first hidden layer has $N_1 = 1000$ activations.\nThe second hidden layer has $N_2 = 10$ activations.\nThe output layer has $N_{out} = 1$ activation.\n\nFor an affine transformation (fully connected layer), the number of parameters is given by:\n(number of input features) * (number of output features) + (number of output features)\n\nFor the first hidden layer:\nInput dimension = $D_{in} = 100$\nOutput dimension = $N_1 = 1000$\nNumber of parameters = $(100 \\times 1000) + 1000 = 100000 + 1000 = 101000$\n\nFor the second hidden layer:\nInput dimension = $N_1 = 1000$\nOutput dimension = $N_2 = 10$\nNumber of parameters = $(1000 \\times 10) + 10 = 10000 + 10 = 10010$\n\nFor the output layer:\nInput dimension = $N_2 = 10$\nOutput dimension = $N_{out} = 1$\nNumber of parameters = $(10 \\times 1) + 1 = 10 + 1 = 11$\n\nTotal number of parameters = Parameters in layer 1 + Parameters in layer 2 + Parameters in output layer\nTotal parameters = $101000 + 10010 + 11 = 111021$\n\nComparing this value with the given options:\nA. 120010\nB. 111110\nC. 100121\nD. 112110\nE. 110010\nF. 110020\nG. 122121\nH. 110011\nI. 111021\nJ. 130021\n\nThe calculated total number of parameters is 111021, which matches option I.\n\nThe first hidden layer has $100 \\times 1000$ weights and $1000$ biases, totaling $101000$ parameters. The second hidden layer has $1000 \\times 10$ weights and $10$ biases, totaling $10010$ parameters. The output layer has $10 \\times 1$ weights and $1$ bias, totaling $11$ parameters. The sum is $101000 + 10010 + 11 = 111021$.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{I}$.",
