    "global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9451",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Determine the period of the following signal, $$ x_1(t)=\\cos (3 \\pi t)-4 \\cos (5 \\pi t-0.5 \\pi) $$\n\nOptions: \nA. 3\nB. 4\nC. 0.5\nD. 3.5\nE. 1.5\nF. 1\nG. 5\nH. 2\nI. 2.5\nJ. 6\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The given signal is a sum of two cosine functions:\n$$ x_1(t) = \\cos(3\\pi t) - 4\\cos(5\\pi t - 0.5\\pi) $$\nThe period of a signal of the form $A\\cos(\\omega t + \\phi)$ is $T = \\frac{2\\pi}{\\omega}$.\nFor the first term, $\\cos(3\\pi t)$, the angular frequency is $\\omega_1 = 3\\pi$. Thus, the period is $T_1 = \\frac{2\\pi}{3\\pi} = \\frac{2}{3}$.\nFor the second term, $-4\\cos(5\\pi t - 0.5\\pi)$, the angular frequency is $\\omega_2 = 5\\pi$. Thus, the period is $T_2 = \\frac{2\\pi}{5\\pi} = \\frac{2}{5}$.\nThe period of the sum of two periodic signals is the least common multiple (LCM) of their individual periods.\nWe need to find the LCM of $T_1 = \\frac{2}{3}$ and $T_2 = \\frac{2}{5}$.\nThe LCM of two fractions $\\frac{a}{b}$ and $\\frac{c}{d}$ is given by $\\frac{\\text{LCM}(a, c)}{\\text{GCD}(b, d)}$.\nIn our case, $a=2, b=3, c=2, d=5$.\nLCM(2, 2) = 2.\nGCD(3, 5) = 1.\nTherefore, the period of $x_1(t)$ is $\\frac{\\text{LCM}(2, 2)}{\\text{GCD}(3, 5)} = \\frac{2}{1} = 2$.\n\nThe period of the signal is 2.\n\nLet's check the options.\nThe options are integers or simple fractions.\nA. 3\nB. 4\nC. 0.5\nD. 3.5\nE. 1.5\nF. 1\nG. 5\nH. 2\nI. 2.5\nJ. 6\n\nOur calculated period is 2, which corresponds to option H.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{H}$.",
