    "global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9466",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Suppose that a certain software product has a mean time between failures of 10,000 hours and has a mean time to repair of 20 hours. If the product is used by 100 customers, what is its availability?\n\nOptions: \nA. 90%\nB. 97%\nC. 100%\nD. 75%\nE. 85%\nF. 99%\nG. 80%\nH. 95%\nI. 98%\nJ. 99.80%\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The availability of a system is calculated using the formula: Availability = MTBF / (MTBF + MTTR), where MTBF is the Mean Time Between Failures and MTTR is the Mean Time To Repair.  In this case, MTBF = 10,000 hours and MTTR = 20 hours. The number of customers does not directly affect the availability calculation for a single product instance.\n\nAvailability = 10,000 hours / (10,000 hours + 20 hours) = 10,000 / 10,020 ≈ 0.99800399... or 99.80%.\n\nTherefore, the most likely correct answer is 99.80%.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
      "success": true,
