      "generated_answer": "The minimal-degree interpolating polynomial for $n+1$ distinct data points is unique. For $n+1$ data points, the highest possible degree of the interpolating polynomial is $n$. This is because a polynomial of degree $n$ can pass through $n+1$ distinct points. If we try a polynomial of degree $n+1$ or higher, there will be infinitely many such polynomials, and therefore it would not be the minimal-degree interpolating polynomial.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{G}$.",
