\nWe are looking for the minimum vertex cover. The sizes are 3, 3, 2, 3.\nThe minimum size is 2, obtained by [0, 4].\nCheck if [0, 4] is a valid vertex cover.\nEdges: (0,2), (2,4), (3,4), (1,4).\nVertex cover {0, 4}.\n(0,2) is covered by 0. Yes.\n(2,4) is covered by 4. Yes.\n(3,4) is covered by 4. Yes.\n(1,4) is covered by 4. Yes.\nSo, [0, 4] is a vertex cover of size 2.\nThe other options are of size 3. Therefore, [0, 4] is the minimum vertex cover given that 0 is in the cover.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{D}$.",
