      "generated_answer": "The most likely answer is **D. Step size is too large**.\n\nIf the training loss increases with epochs, it suggests that the model is not converging and might be oscillating or diverging. A step size that is too large (learning rate) can cause the optimization algorithm to overshoot the minimum, preventing convergence and leading to increasing loss. Regularization issues (A, F) and model complexity issues (G, I) are more related to overfitting or underfitting, which would typically manifest as a plateau or a decreasing trend in training loss with potentially divergence in validation loss. Epoch count (B, E) and data shuffling (H) are important, but a constantly increasing training loss is a stronger indicator of a learning rate problem.",
