    "global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9260",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which is the smallest asymptotically?\n\nOptions: \nA. O(n^2)\nB. O(sqrt(n))\nC. O(1)\nD. O(n^1/2)\nE. O(2^n)\nF. O(log n)\nG. O(n)\nH. O(n log n)\nI. O(n!)\nJ. O(n^3)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The question asks to identify the smallest asymptotically among the given options. Asymptotic notation describes the limiting behavior of a function as the input approaches infinity. The order of growth from smallest to largest is generally: $O(1) < O(\\log n) < O(\\sqrt{n}) = O(n^{1/2}) < O(n) < O(n \\log n) < O(n^2) < O(n^3) < O(2^n) < O(n!)$.\n\nComparing the options based on this order:\nA. $O(n^2)$\nB. $O(\\sqrt{n})$\nC. $O(1)$\nD. $O(n^{1/2})$ which is the same as $O(\\sqrt{n})$, so options B and D are equivalent.\nE. $O(2^n)$\nF. $O(\\log n)$\nG. $O(n)$\nH. $O(n \\log n)$\nI. $O(n!)$\nJ. $O(n^3)$\n\nThe smallest among these is $O(1)$, which represents a constant growth rate.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{C}$.",
