    "cost": null,
    "accuracy": null
  },
  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9257",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a certain country, a person must be at least 16 years old to drive a car and must be at least 18 years old to vote. The variable age represents the age of a person as an integer. Which of the following expressions evaluates to true if the person is old enough to drive but not old enough to vote, and evaluates to false otherwise?\n I. (age ≥ 16) AND (age ≤ 18)\n II. (age ≥ 16) AND (NOT(age ≥ 18))\n III. (age < 18) AND (NOT(age < 16))\n\nOptions: \nA. II only\nB. I and II only\nC. I and III only\nD. II and III only\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let's analyze each expression:\n\nExpression I: (age ≥ 16) AND (age ≤ 18)\nThis expression evaluates to true if the person's age is 16, 17, or 18. The condition \"not old enough to vote\" means age < 18. So this expression is not correct because it includes age 18.\n\nExpression II: (age ≥ 16) AND (NOT(age ≥ 18))\nThis expression means the person is at least 16 years old AND it is NOT true that they are 18 or older. This simplifies to age ≥ 16 AND age < 18, meaning the age can be 16 or 17. This fits the criteria of being old enough to drive (≥ 16) but not old enough to vote (< 18).\n\nExpression III: (age < 18) AND (NOT(age < 16))\nThis expression means the person is younger than 18 AND it is NOT true that they are younger than 16. This simplifies to age < 18 AND age ≥ 16, meaning the age can be 16 or 17. This also fits the criteria.\n\nTherefore, expressions II and III correctly evaluate to true under the given conditions.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{D}$.",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 221,
