      "generated_answer": "The range for an 8-bit word representation depends on the system.\n\nIn two's complement, the range for an 8-bit word is -128 to 127.\n109 is within this range.\n-42 is within this range.\n109 + (-42) = 67, which is also within the range.\n\nIn sign and magnitude, the range for an 8-bit word is -127 to 127.\n109 is within this range.\n-42 is within this range.\n109 + (-42) = 67, which is also within the range.\n\nIn one's complement, the range for an 8-bit word is -127 to 127.\n109 is within this range.\n-42 is within this range.\n109 + (-42) = 67, which is also within the range.\n\nTherefore, addition of 109 and -42 is within range for all three representations.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{B}$.",
