    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is **D**.\n\nBagging, or bootstrap aggregating, uses multiple weak classifiers trained on different bootstrapped samples of the data. By averaging the predictions of these weak learners, bagging reduces the variance and thus prevents overfitting. Options that involve not sampling or using strong classifiers would increase the risk of overfitting.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{D}$.",
