    "global index": "MMLUPro_philosophy_9691",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Identify the antecedent of the following conditional proposition: When the university raises tuition, then either the governor approves of it or the board of trustees doesn't prevent it.\n\nOptions: \nA. The board of trustees prevents it.\nB. The university raises tuition.\nC. The board of trustees approves it.\nD. The governor and the board of trustees don't prevent it.\nE. The governor approves of it.\nF. The board of trustees doesn't prevent it.\nG. The governor and the board of trustees prevent it.\nH. The governor disapproves of it.\nI. The university doesn't raise tuition.\nJ. The university lowers tuition.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
