    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Why is an array of equally spaced dots perceived asrows and columns ?\n\nOptions: \nA. Perception of rows and columns is due to the magnetic field of the Earth influencing visual processing.\nB. The dots are perceived as rows and columns due to color contrast.\nC. It is because the human brain is programmed to recognize faces, and this pattern is similar to facial features.\nD. The dots are seen in rows and columns because of the repetitive motion in which the observer moves their eyes.\nE. Columns and rows are organized figures that the eye sees easily and it tends to organize unconnected, yet closely placed objects into a familiar pattern.\nF. The dots form a grid pattern due to the optical illusion caused by light refraction.\nG. The perception is due to the varying size of the dots.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
