    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When the corpus callosum is cut in a right-handed patient, often the patient\n\nOptions: \nA. Cannot name objects placed in the right hand if the patient can see them\nB. cannot recognize objects placed in the right hand\nC. cannot name objects placed in the left hand if the patient cannot see them\nD. cannot carry out well-learned motor tasks with the left hand\nE. shows a decline in verbal intelligence\nF. loses the ability to speak\nG. Cannot name objects placed in the right hand if the patient cannot see them\nH. cannot carry out well-learned motor tasks with the right hand\nI. shows a decline in spatial intelligence\nJ. can no longer write with their right hand\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is C.\n\nWhen the corpus callosum is cut, the two hemispheres of the brain can no longer communicate effectively. For a right-handed patient, language processing is primarily in the left hemisphere. If an object is placed in the left hand and the patient cannot see it, the sensory information goes to the right hemisphere, which cannot transfer this information to the left (language-dominant) hemisphere for naming.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{C}$",
