  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2209",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Pilocarpineis a drug that stimulates the nerve endings of parasympatheticnerves. What effects would you expect this drugto have on (a) the digestive tract, (b) the iris of the eye, and(c) the heart rate?\n\nOptions: \nA. (a) Digestion would be slightly enhanced, (b) the pupil size would not change, (c) the heart rate would decrease moderately.\nB. (a) No significant effect on digestion, (b) the pupil would constrict, (c) the heart rate would increase markedly.\nC. (a) Digestion would become highly irregular, (b) the pupil would constrict slightly, (c) the heart rate would increase dramatically.\nD. (a) Digestion would be slightly inhibited, (b) the pupil would dilate, (c) the heart rate would remain unchanged.\nE. (a) Digestion is facilitated or enhanced, (b) the pupil would reduce in size, (c) the heart beat would slow and weaken.\nF. (a) Digestion is inhibited, (b) the pupil would enlarge, (c) the heart beat would increase and strengthen.\nG. (a) Digestion would be unaffected, (b) the pupil would fluctuate in size, (c) the heart rate would decrease slightly.\nH. (a) Digestion would slow down, (b) the pupil would remain the same size, (c) the heart beat would quicken.\nI. (a) Digestion would speed up dramatically, (b) the pupil would dilate significantly, (c) the heart rate would increase slightly.\nJ. (a) Digestion remains unaffected, (b) the pupil would dilate, (c) the heart beat would remain the same.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Pilocarpine is a parasympathomimetic drug, meaning it mimics the action of the parasympathetic nervous system. The parasympathetic nervous system generally promotes \"rest and digest\" functions. This includes increasing gastrointestinal motility, constricting the pupil (miosis), and decreasing heart rate. Therefore, we expect enhanced digestion, pupillary constriction, and a reduced heart rate.\n\nComparing these expectations to the options:\n(a) Digestion is facilitated or enhanced.\n(b) The pupil would reduce in size (constrict).\n(c) The heart beat would slow and weaken (decrease in rate and force).\n\nOption E aligns with these effects.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{E}$.",
