      "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is **B**.\n\nWhite matter is primarily composed of myelinated axons, which appear white due to the myelin sheath. These axons form nerve fiber pathways that connect different areas of the central nervous system. Gray matter, on the other hand, consists mainly of neuron cell bodies (somas), dendrites, unmyelinated axons, and glial cells. This combination gives it a grayish appearance. Options A, C, D, E, F, G, H, and I are incorrect because they either misrepresent the composition of white and gray matter or their distribution.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{B}$.",
