  {
    "global index": "MMLU_formal_logic_16",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Identify the antecedent of the following conditional proposition: The university raises tuition if, and only if, both the governor approves of it and the board of trustees recommends it.\n\nOptions: \nA. The university raises tuition.\nB. The governor approves of it.\nC. The board of trustees recommends it.\nD. None of the above\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is **D**.\n\nThe question is about identifying the antecedent of a conditional proposition. The phrase \"if, and only if\" indicates a biconditional (\"iff\") statement. In a biconditional statement, there isn't a single antecedent and consequent in the same way there is in a simple \"if...then\" conditional. Both parts are mutually dependent. If the statement were simply \"A if B,\" then B would be the antecedent. However, with \"A if and only if B,\" it means (A -> B) and (B -> A). Therefore, none of the options alone represents the single antecedent of the entire biconditional.",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 129,
        "output_tokens": 136,
        "total_tokens": 265
      },
      "provider": "openrouter",
      "error": null
    },
