    "accuracy": null
  },
  {
    "global index": "MMLU_formal_logic_37",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Identify the antecedent of the following conditional proposition: The university raises tuition if both the governor approves of it and the board of trustees recommends it.\n\nOptions: \nA. The university raises tuition.\nB. The governor approves of it.\nC. The board of trustees recommends it.\nD. The governor approves of it and the board of trustees recommends it.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is D.\n\nIn a conditional statement \"if P then Q,\" P is the antecedent and Q is the consequent. The given proposition states \"The university raises tuition **if** both the governor approves of it and the board of trustees recommends it.\" Rewriting this in the standard \"if P then Q\" format, we get \"If both the governor approves of it and the board of trustees recommends it, then the university raises tuition.\" Therefore, the antecedent is \"both the governor approves of it and the board of trustees recommends it.\"\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{D}$",
      "success": true,
