      "generated_answer": "Here's the breakdown of the provided premises and how to arrive at the correct answer:\n\n**Premises:**\n1.  E ⊃ ~F (If E, then not F)\n2.  ~F ⊃ G (If not F, then G)\n3.  ~G (Not G)\n\nWe need to find an immediate consequence. Let's examine the options:\n\n*   We can use Modus Tollens on premise 2 and premise 3.\n    *   Premise 2: ~F ⊃ G\n    *   Premise 3: ~G\n    *   Modus Tollens states that if P ⊃ Q is true and ~Q is true, then ~P must be true.\n    *   Applying this, if ~F ⊃ G is true and ~G is true, then ~(~F) must be true.\n    *   ~~F is equivalent to F.\n\nNow let's look at the options:\n\nA.  E ⊃ F: This is not an immediate consequence.\nB.  F ⊃ G: This is not an immediate consequence.\nC.  G ⊃ E: This is not an immediate consequence.\nD.  ~~F: As shown above, this is an immediate consequence by applying Modus Tollens to premise 2 and premise 3.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{D}$.",
