    "global index": "MMLU_formal_logic_114",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Which of the given formulas of PL is the best symbolization of the following sentence?\nEither England's importing beef is a necessary condition for France's subsidizing agriculture or China promotes human rights given that South Africa doesn't supply diamonds.\n\nOptions: \nA. (E ⊃ F) ∨ (C ≡ ~S)\nB. (F ⊃ E) ∨ (~S ≡ C)\nC. (E ⊃ F) ∨ (S ⊃~C)\nD. (F ⊃ E) ∨ (~S ⊃ C)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
