  {
    "global index": "MMLU_formal_logic_22",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Select the best English interpretation of the given proposition, using the following translation key: Ax: x is an apartment Hx: x is a house Lx: x is large Bxy: x is bigger than y (∀x){{Ax ⊃ (∀y)[(Hy • Ly) ⊃ ∼Bxy]}}\n\nOptions: \nA. All apartments are not bigger than some large house.\nB. No apartment is bigger than any large house.\nC. All large houses are not bigger than some apartment.\nD. No large house is bigger than all apartments.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The given proposition is (∀x){{Ax ⊃ (∀y)[(Hy • Ly) ⊃ ∼Bxy]}}.\nLet's break it down:\n- (∀x) means \"For all x\".\n- Ax means \"x is an apartment\".\n- ⊃ means \"implies\".\n- (∀y) means \"For all y\".\n- Hy means \"y is a house\".\n- Ly means \"y is large\".\n- • means \"and\".\n- ∼ means \"not\".\n- Bxy means \"x is bigger than y\".\n\nSo, the proposition can be read as: \"For all x, if x is an apartment, then for all y, if y is a large house, then it is not the case that x is bigger than y.\"\n\nThis translates to: \"For all apartments x, and for all large houses y, x is not bigger than y.\"\nThis is equivalent to \"No apartment is bigger than any large house.\"\n\nLet's analyze the options:\nA. All apartments are not bigger than some large house. (This would allow for some large houses to be smaller than some apartments.)\nB. No apartment is bigger than any large house. (This directly reflects the meaning of not Bxy for all y that are large houses.)\nC. All large houses are not bigger than some apartment. (This is a different quantification than present in the original formula.)\nD. No large house is bigger than all apartments. (This is also a different quantification.)\n\nTherefore, option B is the best interpretation.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 180,
        "output_tokens": 337,
        "total_tokens": 517
