  {
    "global index": "MMLU_formal_logic_69",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Select the best English interpretation of the given arguments in predicate logic.\n(∃x)(Cx • Ox)\n(∀x)[(~Cx ⊃ ~Bx) ⊃ ~Og]\t/ ~Og\n\nOptions: \nA. Some cookies have oatmeal. If something's not being a cookie entails that it doesn't have chocolate chips, then this cookie doesn't have oatmeal. So this cookie doesn't have oatmeal.\nB. Some cookies have oatmeal. If something is not a cookie and does not have chocolate chips, it doesn't have oatmeal. So this cookie doesn't have oatmeal.\nC. Some cookies have oatmeal. If something doesn't have oatmeal, then it is not a cookie and it doesn't have chocolate chips. So this cookie doesn't have oatmeal.\nD. Some cookies have oatmeal. If something's not having chocolate chips entails that it is not a cookie, then it doesn't have oatmeal. So this cookie doesn't have oatmeal.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The premise (∃x)(Cx • Ox) translates to \"Some cookies have oatmeal.\"\n\nThe premise (∀x)[(~Cx ⊃ ~Bx) ⊃ ~Og] translates to \"For all x, if not being a cookie implies not having chocolate chips, then this specific item (referred to by 'g') does not have oatmeal.\"\n\nThe conclusion is ~Og, which means \"This specific item does not have oatmeal.\"\n\nAnalyzing the options:\n\n*   **A.** \"Some cookies have oatmeal. If something's not being a cookie entails that it doesn't have chocolate chips, then this cookie doesn't have oatmeal. So this cookie doesn't have oatmeal.\" This option correctly translates the premises and conclusion. (~Cx ⊃ ~Bx) means \"not being a cookie implies not having chocolate chips\". The conditional in the second premise is applied to an unspecified \"this cookie\", but the structure of the argument in predicate logic is about universal quantification, which can be applied to any instance. The conclusion ~Og is a statement about a specific instance.\n\n*   **B.** This modifies the second premise to \"If something is not a cookie and does not have chocolate chips, it doesn't have oatmeal.\" This is not the correct interpretation of (~Cx ⊃ ~Bx).\n\n*   **C.** This incorrectly interprets (~Cx ⊃ ~Bx) as (~Ox ⊃ (~Cx • ~Bx)).\n\n*   **D.** This incorrectly interprets (~Cx ⊃ ~Bx) as (~Bx ⊃ ~Cx).\n\nTherefore, option A provides the best English interpretation. Note that the conclusion ~Og is a statement about a specific entity 'g', and the context provided by the question implies this 'g' is meant to be a cookie. While the predicate logic itself doesn't explicitly state 'g' is a cookie within the premises, the phrasing of the options (especially \"this cookie\") suggests it.\n\nThe correct answer is \\boxed{A}.",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 268,
        "output_tokens": 407,
        "total_tokens": 675
      },
      "provider": "openrouter",
      "error": null
    },
    "cost": null,
    "accuracy": null
  },
  {
    "global index": "MMLU_formal_logic_49",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Select the best English interpretation of the given arguments in predicate logic.\nDh ⊃ ~Pt\n(∀x)Px ∨ (∀x)Mx\n~Mb\t/ ~Dh\n\nOptions: \nA. If my headache is dualist state, then your tickle is a physical state. Either everything is physical or everything is mental. But my broken toe is not a mental state. So my headache is not a dualist state.\nB. If my headache is dualist state, then your tickle is not a physical state. Either everything is physical or everything is mental. But my broken toe is not a mental state. So my headache is not a dualist state.\nC. If my headache is dualist state, then your tickle is not a physical state. If everything is physical then everything is mental. But my broken toe is not a mental state. So my headache is not a dualist state.\nD. If my headache is dualist state, then your tickle is not a physical state. Everything is either physical or mental. But my broken toe is not a mental state. So my headache is not a dualist state.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let's break down the predicate logic statement and match it to the English interpretations.\n\n*   `Dh ⊃ ~Pt`: \"If Headache is dualist state (`Dh`), then Tickle is not physical state (`~Pt`).\"\n*   `(∀x)Px ∨ (∀x)Mx`: \"For all x, x is Physical (`Px`) OR for all x, x is Mental (`Mx`).\" This means either everything is physical, or everything is mental.\n*   `~Mb`: \"My broken toe (`Mb`) is not a mental state (`~M` applied to `b`).\"\n*   `/ ~Dh`: \"Therefore, my headache (`Dh`) is not a dualist state (`~D` applied to `h`).\"\n\nNow let's evaluate the options:\n\n*   **Option A**: \"If my headache is dualist state, then your tickle is a physical state.\" This contradicts `~Pt`.\n*   **Option B**: \"If my headache is dualist state, then your tickle is not a physical state.\" This matches `Dh ⊃ ~Pt`. \"Either everything is physical or everything is mental.\" This matches `(∀x)Px ∨ (∀x)Mx`. \"But my broken toe is not a mental state.\" This matches `~Mb`. \"So my headache is not a dualist state.\" This matches `/ ~Dh`.\n*   **Option C**: \"If everything is physical then everything is mental.\" This is a conditional statement and not what `(∀x)Px ∨ (∀x)Mx` means.\n*   **Option D**: \"Everything is either physical or mental.\" This implies `(∀x)(Px ∨ Mx)`, which is different from `(∀x)Px ∨ (∀x)Mx`.\n\nOption B is the best interpretation.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 295,
        "output_tokens": 394,
        "total_tokens": 689
      },
      "provider": "openrouter",
