      "generated_answer": "To find the ratio of the investment prior to sale to the pre-tax gain on the sale: \n\n1. The investment prior to sale was $246 million.\n2. The pre-tax gain on the sale was $171 million.\n\nThe ratio is calculated as:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Ratio} = \\frac{\\text{Investment prior to sale}}{\\text{Pre-tax gain}} = \\frac{246}{171}\n\\]\n\nSimplifying this fraction:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Ratio} = \\frac{246}{171} = \\frac{82}{57} \\approx 1.4386\n\\]\n\nThus, the exact ratio expressed as a fraction is \\(\\frac{82}{57}\\). Therefore, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{82}{57}}\n\\]",
