    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: ThomasSidencarries property-damage insurance on his car witha limit of $5,000. He damages Frank Hartman's car in anaccident to the extent of $2,350. How much will his insurancecompany pay?\n\nOptions: \nA. $5,000\nB. $2,650\nC. $4,700 (double the actual damage)\nD. $1,750 (a figure less than the actual damage)\nE. $2,350\nF. $0\nG. $1,350\nH. $3,000 (more than the actual damage but less than the limit)\nI. $2,500 (a rounded figure close to the actual damage)\nJ. $2,000 (slightly less than the actual damage)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
