    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_727",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Record the maturity date for a draft dated (a) November 12 and payable 60 days after date, (b) June 10 and payable 3 months after date, (c) March 3 and payable 30 days after sight if it is accepted March 15, and (d) October 4 and payable 6 months after sight if it is acceptedOctober 25.\n\nOptions: \nA. January 12, September 10, April 14, April 26\nB. January 12, September 8, April 14, April 23\nC. January 10, September 11, April 15, April 26\nD. January 12, September 9, April 13, April 24\nE. January 11, September 12, April 15, April 26\nF. January 13, September 10, April 16, April 27\nG. January 11, September 11, April 13, April 24\nH. January 10, September 9, April 15, April 25\nI. January 13, September 12, April 16, April 27\nJ. January 11, September 10, April 14, April 25\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let's calculate the maturity dates for each draft.\n\n(a) November 12, payable 60 days after date:\nDays remaining in November: 30 - 12 = 18 days.\nDays needed in December: 60 - 18 = 42 days. Since December has 31 days, we need 42 - 31 = 11 days in January.\nMaturity date: January 11.\n\n(b) June 10, payable 3 months after date:\nAdding 3 months to June 10 brings us to September 10.\nMaturity date: September 10.\n\n(c) March 3, payable 30 days after sight, accepted March 15:\nThe \"sight\" is the date of acceptance, which is March 15.\nMaturity date is 30 days after March 15.\nDays remaining in March: 31 - 15 = 16 days.\nDays needed in April: 30 - 16 = 14 days.\nMaturity date: April 14.\n\n(d) October 4, payable 6 months after sight, accepted October 25:\nThe \"sight\" is the date of acceptance, which is October 25.\nAdding 6 months to October 25 brings us to April 25.\nMaturity date: April 25.\n\nCombining the results: January 11, September 10, April 14, April 25.\n\nLooking at the options, option J best matches these calculated dates: January 11, September 10, April 14, April 25.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{J}$.",
