  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_600",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Find the number of single rolls required to paper a room 18 feet long, 12 feet wide, and 10 feet high, allowing for a 10% waste of paper. A single roll consists of 36 square feet of paper. Make allowance for openings, which include one window 3 feet by 8 feet and one door 4 feet by 9 feet.\n\nOptions: \nA. 17 rolls\nB. 20 rolls\nC. 16 rolls\nD. 23 rolls\nE. 14 rolls\nF. 19 rolls\nG. 18 rolls\nH. 21 rolls\nI. 15 rolls\nJ. 22 rolls\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The total surface area of the walls is $2 \\times (18 \\text{ ft} \\times 10 \\text{ ft}) + 2 \\times (12 \\text{ ft} \\times 10 \\text{ ft}) = 360 \\text{ sq ft} + 240 \\text{ sq ft} = 600 \\text{ sq ft}$.\nThe area of the window is $3 \\text{ ft} \\times 8 \\text{ ft} = 24 \\text{ sq ft}$.\nThe area of the door is $4 \\text{ ft} \\times 9 \\text{ ft} = 36 \\text{ sq ft}$.\nThe total area of openings is $24 \\text{ sq ft} + 36 \\text{ sq ft} = 60 \\text{ sq ft}$.\nThe net area to be papered is $600 \\text{ sq ft} - 60 \\text{ sq ft} = 540 \\text{ sq ft}$.\nAllowing for 10% waste, the total paper needed is $540 \\text{ sq ft} \\times 1.10 = 594 \\text{ sq ft}$.\nSince each roll has 36 square feet, the number of rolls required is $\\frac{594 \\text{ sq ft}}{36 \\text{ sq ft/roll}} = 16.5 \\text{ rolls}$.\nSince we cannot buy half a roll, we need to round up to the nearest whole number. Therefore, we need 17 rolls.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{A}$.",
