  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_742",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Round .1476 to (a) 2 decimal places (b) 3 decimal places (c) 1 decimal place.\n\nOptions: \nA. (a) .15 (b) .148 (c) .1\nB. (a) .15 (b) .147 (c) .14\nC. (a) .14 (b) .148 (c) .2\nD. (a) .14 (b) .149 (c) .14\nE. (a) .15 (b) .149 (c) .15\nF. (a) .14 (b) .147 (c) .2\nG. (a) .15 (b) .147 (c) .2\nH. (a) .15 (b) .149 (c) .1\nI. (a) .14 (b) .147 (c) .1\nJ. (a) .14 (b) .148 (c) .15\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To round .1476 to 2 decimal places, we look at the third decimal place. Since it is 7 (which is 5 or greater), we round up the second decimal place, making it .15.\nTo round .1476 to 3 decimal places, we look at the fourth decimal place. Since it is 6 (which is 5 or greater), we round up the third decimal place, making it .148.\nTo round .1476 to 1 decimal place, we look at the second decimal place. Since it is 4 (which is less than 5), we keep the first decimal place as it is, making it .1.\n\nTherefore, the correct rounding is (a) .15, (b) .148, and (c) .1.\n\nComparing this with the given options:\nA. (a) .15 (b) .148 (c) .1. This matches our calculation.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{A}$.",
