    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_79",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What percent is 131 of 42?\n\nOptions: \nA. 125%\nB. 294.4%\nC. 200%\nD. 262.8%\nE. 175.7%\nF. 147.6%\nG. 210.45%\nH. 312.5%\nI. 350%\nJ. 311.9%\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find what percent 131 is of 42, we can set up the proportion:\n$\\frac{131}{42} = \\frac{x}{100}$\nwhere $x$ represents the percentage.\n\nTo solve for $x$, we can cross-multiply:\n$131 \\times 100 = 42 \\times x$\n$13100 = 42x$\n\nNow, divide both sides by 42:\n$x = \\frac{13100}{42}$\n$x \\approx 311.90476$\n\nRounding to one decimal place, we get approximately 311.9%.\n\nComparing this to the given options, option J, 311.9%, is the closest.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{J}$.",
