    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_100",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A loan is made on December 17 for a time period of 120 days. When is it due (not a leap year)?\n\nOptions: \nA. April 15\nB. April 13\nC. April 18\nD. May 15\nE. April 16\nF. April 12\nG. April 17\nH. May 1\nI. March 17\nJ. April 14\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The loan is made on December 17. We need to find the date 120 days later.\n\n*   Remaining days in December: 31 - 17 = 14 days\n*   Days in January: 31 days\n*   Days in February (not a leap year): 28 days\n*   Days in March: 31 days\n\nTotal days accounted for so far: 14 + 31 + 28 + 31 = 104 days.\n\nWe need 120 days, so 120 - 104 = 16 more days. These 16 days fall in April.\n\nTherefore, the due date is April 16.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{E}$",
