    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_40",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Determine the number of men needed to build a boat in 77 days if it takes 36 men 132 days to build one.\n\nOptions: \nA. 84 men\nB. 36 men\nC. 99 men\nD. 132 men\nE. 45 men\nF. 70 men\nG. 62 men\nH. 50 men\nI. 77 men\nJ. 120 men\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The problem describes an inverse relationship between the number of men and the time it takes to build a boat. We can set up a proportion based on the total \"man-days\" required to build the boat.\n\nTotal man-days = (Number of men) * (Number of days)\n\nWe know that 36 men take 132 days to build a boat. So, the total man-days required is:\nTotal man-days = 36 men * 132 days = 4752 man-days\n\nNow, we want to find out how many men (let's call this 'x') are needed to build the same boat in 77 days.\nx men * 77 days = 4752 man-days\n\nTo find 'x', we divide the total man-days by the new number of days:\nx = 4752 man-days / 77 days\nx = 61.714...\n\nSince we cannot have a fraction of a man, and we need to complete the job within 77 days, we must round up to the nearest whole number.\nx = 62 men\n\nLooking at the options, we find 62 men as an exact option.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{G}$.",
