      "generated_answer": "To find the average speed, we need to calculate the total time taken and divide the total distance by the total time.\nThe plane departed at 11:00 a.m. and arrived at 2:30 p.m.\nThe duration of the flight is from 11:00 a.m. to 2:30 p.m., which is 3 hours and 30 minutes, or 3.5 hours.\nThe distance traveled is 540 miles.\nAverage speed = Distance / Time = 540 miles / 3.5 hours.\n\nCalculation:\n540 / 3.5 = 540 / (7/2) = 540 * (2/7) = 1080 / 7 ≈ 154.28 mph.\n\nLet's re-examine the problem statement or options, as the calculated speed is not among the options. It is possible there's a typo in the problem or the options. Let's assume the arrival time might be different.\n\nLet's try to work backwards from the options.\n\nIf the speed was 360 mph (Option A), then time taken = Distance / Speed = 540 / 360 = 1.5 hours.\nIf the flight took 1.5 hours, departing at 11:00 a.m., arrival would be 12:30 p.m., not 2:30 p.m.\n\nIf the speed was 540 mph (Option J), then time taken = Distance / Speed = 540 / 540 = 1 hour.\nIf the flight took 1 hour, departing at 11:00 a.m., arrival would be 12:00 p.m., not 2:30 p.m.\n\nLet's assume the departure time was different. If the flight took 3.5 hours, and the speed was one of the options.\nIf speed = 360 mph, time = 540/360 = 1.5 hours.\nIf speed = 450 mph, time = 540/450 = 1.2 hours.\nIf speed = 330 mph, time = 540/330 ≈ 1.64 hours.\nIf speed = 240 mph, time = 540/240 = 2.25 hours.\nIf speed = 180 mph, time = 540/180 = 3 hours.\nIf the flight took 3 hours, departing at 11:00 a.m., arrival would be 2:00 p.m., not 2:30 p.m.\n\nIf speed = 420 mph, time = 540/420 ≈ 1.28 hours.\nIf speed = 270 mph, time = 540/270 = 2 hours.\nIf speed = 300 mph, time = 540/300 = 1.8 hours.\nIf speed = 600 mph, time = 540/600 = 0.9 hours.\n\nIt seems there's likely an error in the problem statement or the options provided, as our calculated speed of approximately 154.28 mph is not present, and none of the options yield a flight time of 3.5 hours with the given distance.\n\nHowever, if we must choose an answer from the given options, let's re-examine the provided time calculation.\nFrom 11:00 a.m. to 2:30 p.m. is indeed 3 hours and 30 minutes, which is 3.5 hours.\n\nLet's consider if the starting time or ending time is misread.\nIf arrival time was 2:00 p.m., then the flight time is 3 hours. Speed = 540 / 3 = 180 mph (Option E).\nIf arrival time was 2:40 p.m., then the flight time is 3 hours and 40 minutes = 3 + 40/60 = 3 + 2/3 = 11/3 hours. Speed = 540 / (11/3) = 540 * 3 / 11 = 1620 / 11 ≈ 147.27 mph.\n\nIf the departure time was 11:30 a.m. and arrival at 2:30 p.m., then the flight time is 3 hours. Speed = 540 / 3 = 180 mph (Option E).\nThis seems like a plausible scenario, given that 180 mph is an option.\n\nLet's assume the departure time was 11:30 a.m. and arrival time was 2:30 p.m.\nFlight duration = 2:30 p.m. - 11:30 a.m. = 3 hours.\nDistance = 540 miles.\nAverage speed = Distance / Time = 540 miles / 3 hours = 180 mph.\n\nThis matches option E.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{E}$.",
