    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "This question can be solved using the put-call parity relationship for European options. The formula is:\n\n$C + Ke^{-rT} = P + S$\n\nWhere:\n$C$ = Call option premium\n$K$ = Strike price\n$r$ = Risk-free interest rate\n$T$ = Time to expiration\n$P$ = Put option premium\n$S$ = Spot price of the underlying asset\n\nGiven:\n$C = 5$\n$K = 50$\n$r = 0.02$ (annual rate, assume monthly rate is $0.02/12$)\n$T = 1/12$ (one month in years)\n$S = 52$\n\nFirst, calculate the present value of the strike price:\n$Ke^{-rT} = 50 \\times e^{-(0.02/12) \\times (1/12)}$\n$Ke^{-rT} = 50 \\times e^{-0.00013888...}$\n$Ke^{-rT} \\approx 50 \\times (1 - 0.00013888...) \\approx 50 - 0.006944 \\approx 49.993$\n\nNow, rearrange the put-call parity formula to solve for $P$:\n$P = C + Ke^{-rT} - S$\n$P = 5 + 49.993 - 52$\n$P = 2.993$\n\nLooking at the options, option A, 2.92, is the closest value. There might be a slight difference due to rounding or the exact calculation of the continuous compounding. Let's re-calculate $Ke^{-rT}$ with more precision.\n\n$rT = (0.02/12) \\times (1/12) = 0.02/144 \\approx 0.000138888...$\n$e^{-rT} \\approx 0.99986112...$\n$Ke^{-rT} \\approx 50 \\times 0.99986112 \\approx 49.993056$\n\n$P = 5 + 49.993056 - 52 = 2.993056$\n\nLet's consider if the interest rate is meant to be a monthly rate. If the one-month risk-free rate is 2%, then $r=0.02$ and $T=1$.\n$Ke^{-rT} = 50 \\times e^{-0.02 \\times 1} = 50 \\times e^{-0.02} \\approx 50 \\times 0.98019867 \\approx 49.0099$\n$P = 5 + 49.0099 - 52 = 2.0099$\nThis is close to option J, 2.00.\n\nHowever, the problem states \"one-month risk-free rate is 2%\". It is standard convention for an annual rate to be quoted unless specified otherwise. Let's assume the 2% is an annual rate that needs to be compounded for one month.\n\nLet's re-examine the initial calculation where $r=0.02$ is the annual rate and $T=1/12$.\n$P = 5 + 50 \\times e^{-(0.02 \\times 1/12)} - 52$\n$P = 5 + 50 \\times e^{-0.00166667} - 52$\n$P = 5 + 50 \\times 0.99833479 - 52$\n$P = 5 + 49.9167395 - 52$\n$P = 2.9167395$\n\nThis is very close to option A (2.92).\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{A}$.",
      "success": true,
