    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_438",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An investor has utility function $U(x) = x^{{1/4}}$ for salary. He has a new job offer which pays $80,000 with a bonus. The bonus will be $0, $10000, $20000, $30000, $40000, $50000, or $60000, each with equal probability. What is the certainty equivalent value of this job offer?\n\nOptions: \nA. 100000\nB. 108610\nC. 110000\nD. 105000\nE. 90000\nF. 130000\nG. 120000\nH. 85000\nI. 95000\nJ. 115000\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The investor's utility function is $U(x) = x^{1/4}$. The base salary is $80,000. The possible bonus amounts are $0, $10,000, $20,000, $30,000, $40,000, $50,000, or $60,000, each with equal probability. This means there are 7 possible outcomes for the total salary.\n\nThe possible total salaries are:\n$80,000 + 0 = 80,000$\n$80,000 + 10,000 = 90,000$\n$80,000 + 20,000 = 100,000$\n$80,000 + 30,000 = 110,000$\n$80,000 + 40,000 = 120,000$\n$80,000 + 50,000 = 130,000$\n$80,000 + 60,000 = 140,000$\n\nThe expected utility of this job offer is the average of the utilities of these possible outcomes:\n$E[U(x)] = \\frac{1}{7} [U(80000) + U(90000) + U(100000) + U(110000) + U(120000) + U(130000) + U(140000)]$\n$E[U(x)] = \\frac{1}{7} [80000^{1/4} + 90000^{1/4} + 100000^{1/4} + 110000^{1/4} + 120000^{1/4} + 130000^{1/4} + 140000^{1/4}]$\n\nCalculating the terms:\n$80000^{1/4} \\approx 16.8179$\n$90000^{1/4} \\approx 17.3205$\n$100000^{1/4} \\approx 17.7828$\n$110000^{1/4} \\approx 18.2069$\n$120000^{1/4} \\approx 18.6046$\n$130000^{1/4} \\approx 18.9797$\n$140000^{1/4} \\approx 19.3340$\n\nSum of utilities $\\approx 16.8179 + 17.3205 + 17.7828 + 18.2069 + 18.6046 + 18.9797 + 19.3340 \\approx 127.0464$\n\nExpected utility $\\approx \\frac{127.0464}{7} \\approx 18.1495$\n\nThe certainty equivalent (CE) is the amount of salary that would give the investor the same utility as the expected utility. So, we set $U(CE) = E[U(x)]$.\n$CE^{1/4} = E[U(x)]$\n$CE = (E[U(x)])^4$\n$CE \\approx (18.1495)^4$\n$CE \\approx 108610.2$\n\nComparing this value with the given options, option B is the closest.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{B}$.",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 265,
        "output_tokens": 903,
        "total_tokens": 1168
      },
      "provider": "openrouter",
      "error": null
