    "accuracy": null
  },
  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_620",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: For a one-period binomial model for the price of a stock, you are given: (i) The period is one year. (ii) The stock pays no dividends. (iii) u =1.433, where u is one plus the rate of capital gain on the stock if the price goes up.  (iv) d = 0.756 , where d is one plus the rate of capital loss on the stock if the price goes down. (v) The continuously compounded annual expected return on the stock is 10%. What is the true probability of the stock price going up.\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.58\nB. 0.75\nC. 0.55\nD. 0.30\nE. 0.40\nF. 0.60\nG. 0.65\nH. 0.70\nI. 0.52\nJ. 0.45\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The true probability of the stock price going up, denoted by p, can be calculated using the expected return of the stock. The expected stock price at the end of the period is given by $S_0 * (p*u + (1-p)*d)*e^{rt}$, where $S_0$ is the current stock price, r is the continuously compounded annual expected return, and t is the time period. In this case, t = 1 and r = 0.10. The expected return is also given by $E[S_1] = S_0 * e^{rt}$.\n\nTherefore, we have the equation:\n$p*u + (1-p)*d = e^{rt}$\n\nSubstituting the given values:\n$p*1.433 + (1-p)*0.756 = e^{0.10*1}$\n$1.433p + 0.756 - 0.756p = e^{0.10}$\n$0.677p + 0.756 = 1.10517$\n$0.677p = 1.10517 - 0.756$\n$0.677p = 0.34917$\n$p = 0.34917 / 0.677$\n$p \\approx 0.515758$\n\nLooking at the options, the closest value to 0.515758 is 0.52.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{I}$.",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 269,
        "output_tokens": 358,
        "total_tokens": 627
      },
      "provider": "openrouter",
