    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_441",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Assume that the Black-Scholes framework holds. The price of a nondividened-paying stock is $30. The price of a put option on this stock is $4.00. You are given $(i) $\\Delta=-0.28$. (ii) $\\Gamma=0.10$ Using the delta-gamma approximation, determine the price of the put option if the stock price changes to $31.50.\n\nOptions: \nA. 5.5\nB. 2.9\nC. 4.8\nD. 3.0\nE. 3.7\nF. 4.5\nG. 5.0\nH. 2.5\nI. 4.2\nJ. 3.9\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The delta-gamma approximation for the change in option price ($\\Delta C$) is given by:\n$\\Delta C \\approx \\Delta \\cdot \\Delta S + \\frac{1}{2} \\Gamma \\cdot (\\Delta S)^2$\n\nIn this case, the initial stock price ($S_0$) is $30, the new stock price ($S_1$) is $31.50, so the change in stock price ($\\Delta S$) is $31.50 - 30 = 1.50$.\nWe are given $\\Delta = -0.28$ and $\\Gamma = 0.10$.\nThe initial price of the put option ($P_0$) is $4.00.\n\nNow, let's calculate the change in the put option price:\n$\\Delta P \\approx (-0.28) \\cdot (1.50) + \\frac{1}{2} (0.10) \\cdot (1.50)^2$\n$\\Delta P \\approx -0.42 + \\frac{1}{2} (0.10) \\cdot (2.25)$\n$\\Delta P \\approx -0.42 + 0.05 \\cdot 2.25$\n$\\Delta P \\approx -0.42 + 0.1125$\n$\\Delta P \\approx -0.3075$\n\nThe new price of the put option ($P_1$) is the initial price plus the change in price:\n$P_1 = P_0 + \\Delta P$\n$P_1 \\approx 4.00 + (-0.3075)$\n$P_1 \\approx 3.6925$\n\nLooking at the options, 3.7 is the closest value.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{E}$.",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 226,
        "output_tokens": 406,
        "total_tokens": 632
      },
