    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_635",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How many 9-inch-by-9-inch tiles are needed to cover a floor which is 9 feet long and 6 feet wide? Find the cost if each tile costs 75 cents.\n\nOptions: \nA. 98 tiles, $73.50\nB. 90 tiles, $67.50\nC. 104 tiles, $78.00\nD. 88 tiles, $66.00\nE. 96 tiles, $72.00\nF. 92 tiles, $69.00\nG. 100 tiles, $75.00\nH. 110 tiles, $82.50\nI. 102 tiles, $76.50\nJ. 94 tiles, $70.50\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To solve this problem, we first need to ensure all measurements are in the same units. Since the tiles are measured in inches and the floor in feet, we will convert the floor dimensions to inches.\nThe floor is 9 feet long, which is $9 \\text{ feet} \\times 12 \\text{ inches/foot} = 108 \\text{ inches}$.\nThe floor is 6 feet wide, which is $6 \\text{ feet} \\times 12 \\text{ inches/foot} = 72 \\text{ inches}$.\nThe area of the floor is $108 \\text{ inches} \\times 72 \\text{ inches} = 7776 \\text{ square inches}$.\nEach tile has an area of $9 \\text{ inches} \\times 9 \\text{ inches} = 81 \\text{ square inches}$.\nThe number of tiles needed is the area of the floor divided by the area of one tile: $7776 \\text{ sq in} / 81 \\text{ sq in/tile} = 96 \\text{ tiles}$.\nThe cost of each tile is 75 cents, which is $0.75.\nThe total cost is the number of tiles multiplied by the cost per tile: $96 \\text{ tiles} \\times \\$0.75\\text{/tile} = \\$72.00$.\nTherefore, 96 tiles are needed to cover the floor, and the total cost will be $72.00.\n\nComparing this to the given options:\nA. 98 tiles, $73.50\nB. 90 tiles, $67.50\nC. 104 tiles, $78.00\nD. 88 tiles, $66.00\nE. 96 tiles, $72.00\nF. 92 tiles, $69.00\nG. 100 tiles, $75.00\nH. 110 tiles, $82.50\nI. 102 tiles, $76.50\nJ. 94 tiles, $70.50\n\nOption E matches our calculated answer.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{E}$.",
      "success": true,
