    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Here's how to solve the problem:\n\n1.  **Calculate the wall area:** The room has four walls. Two walls are 14' by 8.5' and two are 10' by 8.5'.\n    *   Area of two 14' walls: 2 \\* (14 ft \\* 8.5 ft) = 2 \\* 119 sq ft = 238 sq ft\n    *   Area of two 10' walls: 2 \\* (10 ft \\* 8.5 ft) = 2 \\* 85 sq ft = 170 sq ft\n    *   Total wall area: 238 sq ft + 170 sq ft = 408 sq ft\n\n2.  **Calculate the number of quarts needed:** One quart covers 36 sq ft.\n    *   Number of quarts = Total wall area / Coverage per quart\n    *   Number of quarts = 408 sq ft / 36 sq ft/quart = 11.33 quarts\n\n3.  **Determine the actual quarts to buy:** Since you can't buy fractions of quarts, James needs to buy 12 quarts.\n\n4.  **Calculate the cost of paint:** Each quart costs $9.80.\n    *   Paint cost = Number of quarts \\* Cost per quart\n    *   Paint cost = 12 quarts \\* $9.80/quart = $117.60\n\n5.  **Calculate the labor cost:** Labor costs $5 per quart or fraction thereof. Since he needs 12 quarts, he will pay for 12 units of labor.\n    *   Labor cost = Number of quarts \\* Labor cost per quart\n    *   Labor cost = 12 quarts \\* $5/quart = $60.00\n\n6.  **Calculate the total cost:**\n    *   Total cost = Paint cost + Labor cost\n    *   Total cost = $117.60 + $60.00 = $177.60\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{D}$.",
