    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_706",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the refund on an insurance policy with anannual premiumof $37 that is canceled 33 days after it was purchased?\n\nOptions: \nA. $28.40\nB. $30.50\nC. $7.40\nD. $34.60\nE. $31.10\nF. $32.20\nG. $25.00\nH. $29.60\nI. $35.60\nJ. $33.70\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To determine the refund, we need to calculate the amount of premium that has been used. The policy has been active for 33 days out of a 365-day year. The portion of the premium used is $(33/365) * $37. The refund is the total premium minus the used portion: Refund = $37 - (33/365) * $37$.\n\nCalculating the used portion:\nUsed portion = $(33 / 365) * 37$\nUsed portion $\\approx 0.09041 * 37$\nUsed portion $\\approx 3.34517$\n\nCalculating the refund:\nRefund = $37 - 3.34517$\nRefund $\\approx 33.65483$\n\nRounding to two decimal places, the refund is approximately $33.65. Looking at the options, $33.70 is the closest value.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{J}$.",
