    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_210",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Ms. Edwards' disposable income (that is, her income after taxes have been paid) has risen from $19,000 to $20,000. Her expenditures have risen from $15,200 to $15,950. 1) What is her marginal propensity to consume? 2) What is her marginal propensity to save?\n\nOptions: \nA. Marginal propensity to consume is .70, marginal propensity to save is .30\nB. Marginal propensity to consume is .80, marginal propensity to save is .20\nC. Marginal propensity to consume is .95, marginal propensity to save is .05\nD. Marginal propensity to consume is .85, marginal propensity to save is .15\nE. Marginal propensity to consume is .75, marginal propensity to save is .25\nF. Marginal propensity to consume is .50, marginal propensity to save is .50\nG. Marginal propensity to consume is .55, marginal propensity to save is .45\nH. Marginal propensity to consume is .60, marginal propensity to save is .40\nI. Marginal propensity to consume is .65, marginal propensity to save is .35\nJ. Marginal propensity to consume is 1.00, marginal propensity to save is 0.00\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To calculate the marginal propensity to consume (MPC), we find the change in consumption divided by the change in disposable income.\nMPC = (Change in Expenditures) / (Change in Disposable Income)\nMPC = ($15,950 - $15,200) / ($20,000 - $19,000)\nMPC = $750 / $1,000\nMPC = 0.75\n\nThe marginal propensity to save (MPS) is 1 minus the MPC.\nMPS = 1 - MPC\nMPS = 1 - 0.75\nMPS = 0.25\n\nTherefore, the marginal propensity to consume is 0.75 and the marginal propensity to save is 0.25.\n\nComparing this to the given options, option E matches our calculated values.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{E}$.",
