  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_692",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Calculate the Gross Domestic Product using the total expenditure approach:\nConsumption Expenditures | $500 billion\nWages and salaries | $400 billion\n(Gross Private) Investments Expenditures | $80 billion\nGovernment Expenditures | $100 billion\nTaxes | $70 billion\nImports | $50 billion\nExports | $30 billion\nWhat is the GDP (in billions)?\n\nOptions: \nA. 700\nB. 730\nC. 710\nD. 760\nE. 640\nF. 680\nG. 650\nH. 720\nI. 750\nJ. 660\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The Gross Domestic Product (GDP) using the expenditure approach is calculated as C + I + G + (X - M), where C is Consumption Expenditures, I is Investment Expenditures, G is Government Expenditures, X is Exports, and M is Imports.\n\nGiven:\nConsumption Expenditures (C) = $500 billion\nInvestment Expenditures (I) = $80 billion\nGovernment Expenditures (G) = $100 billion\nExports (X) = $30 billion\nImports (M) = $50 billion\n\nWages and salaries, taxes, and imports are not directly used in the expenditure approach calculation for GDP.\n\nGDP = C + I + G + (X - M)\nGDP = $500 billion + $80 billion + $100 billion + ($30 billion - $50 billion)\nGDP = $500 billion + $80 billion + $100 billion - $20 billion\nGDP = $680 billion - $20 billion\nGDP = $660 billion\n\nTherefore, the GDP is $660 billion.\n\nThe correct answer is J.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{J}$.",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 214,
        "output_tokens": 248,
