  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_278",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Friedman Brothers accepted a 60-day sight draft on April 10, for $562.50. It was discounted on April 15 at 6%, find the proceeds.\n\nOptions: \nA. $562.50\nB. $557.34\nC. $560.00\nD. $555.34\nE. $559.90\nF. $550.00\nG. $558.50\nH. $553.25\nI. $5.16\nJ. $565.75\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The problem involves calculating the proceeds of a discounted sight draft.\n\n1.  **Calculate the maturity date:** A 60-day sight draft accepted on April 10 means the maturity date is 60 days after April 10.\n    *   April has 30 days. So, 30 days remaining in April (30 - 10 = 20 days).\n    *   May has 31 days.\n    *   June has 30 days.\n    *   Starting from April 10:\n        *   April: 20 days (April 11 to April 30)\n        *   May: 31 days\n        *   Total days so far: 20 + 31 = 51 days.\n        *   Remaining days needed: 60 - 51 = 9 days.\n        *   So, the maturity date is June 9. (This is 60 days *after* April 10, meaning the draft is payable on June 9).\n\n2.  **Calculate the discount period:** The draft was discounted on April 15. The discount period is the number of days from the discount date to the maturity date.\n    *   Days remaining in April: From April 15 to April 30 = 16 days (30 - 15 + 1).\n    *   Days in May: 31 days.\n    *   Days in June: 9 days (up to June 9).\n    *   Total discount period = 16 + 31 + 9 = 56 days.\n\n3.  **Calculate the discount amount:**\n    *   Face Value (FV) = $562.50\n    *   Discount Rate (R) = 6% = 0.06\n    *   Discount Period (T) = 56 days / 360 (since it's a financial calculation, typically a 360-day year is used unless specified otherwise)\n    *   Discount = FV * R * T = $562.50 * 0.06 * (56 / 360)\n    *   Discount = $562.50 * 0.06 * 0.155555...\n    *   Discount = $5.25\n\n4.  **Calculate the proceeds:**\n    *   Proceeds = Face Value - Discount\n    *   Proceeds = $562.50 - $5.25\n    *   Proceeds = $557.25\n\nNow, let's re-check the maturity date and discount period carefully.\nA 60-day sight draft accepted on April 10 means it is payable 60 days after April 10.\nSo, the due date is:\nApril: 30 - 10 = 20 days.\nMay: 31 days.\n20+31 = 51 days.\nRemaining days needed: 60 - 51 = 9 days. So, June 9 is the maturity date.\n\nThe draft was discounted on April 15. The discount period is from April 15 to June 9.\nDays in April from April 15: 30 - 15 = 15 days.\nDays in May: 31 days.\nDays in June: 9 days.\nTotal discount period = 15 + 31 + 9 = 55 days.\n\nDiscount = Principal * Rate * Time\nDiscount = $562.50 * 0.06 * (55 / 360)\nDiscount = $562.50 * 0.06 * 0.152777...\nDiscount = $5.16\n\nProceeds = Face Value - Discount\nProceeds = $562.50 - $5.16\nProceeds = $557.34\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{B}$\nThe maturity date is June 9. The discount period from April 15 to June 9 is 55 days. The discount amount is $562.50 * 0.06 * (55/360) = $5.16, making the proceeds $562.50 - $5.16 = $557.34.",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 202,
        "output_tokens": 980,
        "total_tokens": 1182
      },
      "provider": "openrouter",
