    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To express a fraction as a percentage, multiply the fraction by 100%.\n\nFor the first fraction, (2/5):\n(2/5) * 100% = (2 * 100) / 5 % = 200 / 5 % = 40%.\n\nFor the second fraction, [1/(100)]:\n[1/(100)] * 100% = (1 * 100) / 100 % = 100 / 100 % = 1%.\n\nTherefore, (2/5) as a percentage is 40%, and [1/(100)] as a percentage is 1%.\n\nComparing this to the given options:\nOption B matches our results: 40%, 1%.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{B}$.",
