    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_232",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Nelson's Cycle Shop had a January 1 inventory of $30,156. During the month, new merchandise purchases totaled $28,300, and sales totaled $72,600. If the margin on sales was 45%, estimate the final inventory.\n\nOptions: \nA. $28,300\nB. $45,600\nC. $32,670\nD. $22,150\nE. $20,000\nF. $41,200\nG. $18,526\nH. $39,930\nI. $34,850\nJ. $25,400\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "openai/gpt-4o-mini",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the final inventory, we first need to calculate the cost of goods sold (COGS). Given that sales totaled $72,600 and the margin on sales was 45%, the cost of the goods sold can be calculated as follows: \n\nSales - (Sales * Margin) = COGS  \n$72,600 - ($72,600 * 0.45) = $72,600 - $32,670 = $39,930.  \n\nFinally, we find the final inventory by using the formula:  \nFinal Inventory = Beginning Inventory + Purchases - COGS  \nFinal Inventory = $30,156 + $28,300 - $39,930 = $18,526.\n\nThus, the final inventory estimate is \\(\\boxed{G}\\).",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 186,
        "output_tokens": 157,
        "total_tokens": 343
      },
      "provider": "openrouter",
      "error": null
