  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_580",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Owens Company accepted a draft, 90-day sight, amounting to $560 drawn on them by Watts Bros. Watts Bros, had the draft discounted 34 days before the due date at 6%. What were the proceeds?\n\nOptions: \nA. $560\nB. $550.00\nC. $555.00\nD. $558.50\nE. $562.00\nF. $558.00\nG. $563.17\nH. $556.83\nI. $553.83\nJ. $551.67\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Here's how to calculate the proceeds:\n\n1.  **Determine the discount period:** The draft is for 90 days sight. It was discounted 34 days before the due date. So, the discount period is 34 days.\n\n2.  **Calculate the discount amount:**\n    *   Face value of the draft (Principal) = $560\n    *   Annual interest rate = 6% or 0.06\n    *   Time (in years) = 34 days / 365 days ≈ 0.09315 years\n    *   Discount amount = Principal \\* Rate \\* Time\n    *   Discount amount = $560 \\* 0.06 \\* (34/365) ≈ $3.1367\n\n3.  **Calculate the proceeds:**\n    *   Proceeds = Face value of the draft - Discount amount\n    *   Proceeds = $560 - $3.1367 ≈ $556.8633\n\nLooking at the options, $556.83 is the closest to our calculated proceeds.\n\nThe correct answer is **H**.",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 209,
        "output_tokens": 258,
        "total_tokens": 467
      },
      "provider": "openrouter",
      "error": null
