  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_312",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: TheMotorollaElectronics Company is taking inventory. It discovers that it has 30 widgets on hand. Records reveal the following information: Quantity Cost Per Unit Inventory, Dec. 2 6 $2.30 Purchase, Jan. 15 352 $2.50 Purchase, Feb. 4 101 $2.20 Purchase, Feb. 14 645 $2.00 Find the value of widgets in their inventory using the FIFO method of inventory.\n\nOptions: \nA. $120\nB. $45\nC. $55\nD. $30\nE. $85\nF. $60.00\nG. $110\nH. $75\nI. $90\nJ. $100\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the value of widgets using the FIFO (First-In, First-Out) method, we assume that the first widgets purchased are the first ones sold. The company has 30 widgets on hand. We need to consider the most recent purchases first, working backwards until we have accounted for all 30 widgets.\n\nThe purchases were:\n* Inventory, Dec 2: 6 @ $2.30\n* Purchase, Jan 15: 352 @ $2.50\n* Purchase, Feb 4: 101 @ $2.20\n* Purchase, Feb 14: 645 @ $2.00\n\nWe need to fulfill the 30 widgets on hand from the most recent purchases. The most recent purchase is from February 14th at $2.00 per unit. Since we need 30 widgets, and the February 14th purchase is 645 units, we can take all 30 units from this purchase.\n\nValue = 30 widgets * $2.00/widget = $60.00\n\nLooking at the options, $60.00 is provided.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{F}$.",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 234,
        "output_tokens": 263,
        "total_tokens": 497
      },
      "provider": "openrouter",
      "error": null
