  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_682",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  If an advertisement shows the interior of a train with comfortable seats and plenty of space yet a customer boards a train only to find a lack of space and hard seating. This is an example of:\n\nOptions: \nA. GAP 9-the gap between service delivery and customer satisfaction.\nB. GAP 2-the gap between management perception and service-quality specification\nC. GAP 4-the gap between service delivery and external communications.\nD. GAP 5-the gap between customer perception and customer expectation.\nE. GAP 7-the gap between service quality and customer perception.\nF. GAP 3-the gap between service-quality specifications and service delivery.\nG. GAP 10-the gap between service quality and service delivery.\nH. GAP1-the gap between the customer's expectations and management perception.\nI. GAP 6-the gap between customer expectation and management perception.\nJ. GAP 8-the gap between external communications and customer expectation.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The advertisement created an expectation in the customer's mind. The actual experience on the train did not meet that expectation. This discrepancy falls under the gap between what was communicated externally and the customer's actual perception. Therefore, this is an example of GAP 4.\n\nThe advertisement is an external communication. The customer's experience of the train is the service delivery. The discrepancy between the advertised comfort and the actual discomfort is a mismatch between external communications and service delivery. This leads to a negative customer experience because their expectations, set by the advertisement, were not met in reality.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{C}$.",
      "success": true,
