    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_293",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is not an assumption underpinning the rational decision making model?\n\nOptions: \nA. Decisions are made in a vacuum, without influence from outside factors\nB. Decisions are always optimal and maximize utility\nC. The decision maker's preferences are stable and consistent\nD. High level of certainty regarding the environment\nE. Unlimited time for making a decision\nF. A structured problem\nG. Perfect knowledge of all possible options and their outcomes\nH. Incomplete information\nI. An agreed goal\nJ. Rationality of the decision maker\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The rational decision-making model makes several strong assumptions about the decision-maker and the environment. These typically include having complete information, unlimited time, a well-defined problem, stable preferences, and the ability to always make optimal choices. Therefore, anything that contradicts these assumptions is not part of the model.\n\nOption H, \"Incomplete information,\" directly contradicts the assumption of perfect knowledge of all possible options and their outcomes (Option G). The rational decision-making model assumes a high degree of certainty or complete knowledge, not incomplete information.\n\nThe correct answer is **H**.",
