    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_340",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: JamesParcerdiscounted a customer's $500 note on April 25. The note was dated March 1. and must be paid within 3 months of the day issued. What is the term of discount?\n\nOptions: \nA. 65 days\nB. 37 days\nC. 55 days\nD. 25 days\nE. 60 days\nF. 30 days\nG. 45 days\nH. 92 days\nI. 75 days\nJ. 80 days\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The note must be paid within 3 months of March 1st. This means the maturity date is June 1st.\nThe discount date is April 25th. The term of discount is the number of days from the discount date to the maturity date.\nFrom April 25th to June 1st, there are 6 days remaining in April (30 - 25 = 5, so 6 days including the 25th if we count the day of discount, but typically it's the number of days *after* the discount date until maturity), plus 31 days in May, plus 1 day in June. This gives us 6 + 31 + 1 = 38 days.\n\nLet's re-evaluate the counting of days more precisely for discount terms. The term of discount is the number of days between the date of discount and the date of maturity, *excluding* the date of discount but *including* the date of maturity.\n\nMaturity date: 3 months from March 1st is June 1st.\nDiscount date: April 25th.\n\nNumber of days remaining in April: April has 30 days. So, from April 25th to end of April, we have 30 - 25 = 5 days. (These are April 26, 27, 28, 29, 30).\nNumber of days in May: 31 days.\nNumber of days in June until maturity: 1 day (June 1st).\n\nTotal days = 5 (remaining in April) + 31 (in May) + 1 (in June) = 37 days.\n\nLet's check the options provided. Option B is 37 days.\n\nThe question states \"must be paid within 3 months of the day issued\".\nIssued date: March 1.\n3 months from March 1 is June 1. So, the maturity date is June 1.\n\nDiscounted on April 25.\nNumber of days from April 25 to June 1.\n\nDays remaining in April (excluding discount date, including maturity date):\nApril has 30 days.\nDays in April from April 26 to April 30 = 5 days.\nDays in May = 31 days.\nDays in June = 1 day (June 1).\nTotal days = 5 + 31 + 1 = 37 days.\n\nThe term of discount is the number of days the note is held by the discounter until it matures. This is calculated from the day *after* the discount date up to and including the maturity date.\n\nFinal check:\nMaturity date: June 1st.\nDiscount date: April 25th.\n\nDays in April after April 25th: April 26, 27, 28, 29, 30 (5 days).\nDays in May: 31 days.\nDay in June: June 1st (1 day).\nTotal days = 5 + 31 + 1 = 37 days.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{B}$.",
