 for the 45-year-old should be higher than the cost for the 25-year-old. Our calculations based on Option C's annual premiums support this. $2207 for the younger man and $3649 for the older man.\n\nComparing the options again with this understanding:\nOption H. $2207 and $3649. This represents the total cost for the 25-year-old and the 45-year-old, respectively. This is the most logical choice given the information derived from Option C.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{H}$.",
