    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_108",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: It has been found that hours of recreation (r) and wages (W) have a direct effect on productivity (P), so that : P =ar+bW. In two surveys it was found that Survey 1P = 170 : r = 51 : W = 136 Survey 2P = 425 : r = 68 : W = 204 What are the values of a and b ?\n\nOptions: \nA. a = 68, b = 204\nB. a = 2, b = 1.25\nC. a = 0, b = 3\nD. a = 170, b = 425\nE. a = 5, b = 2\nF. a = 4, b = 1.5\nG. a = 3, b = 0.5\nH. a = -20, b = 8.75\nI. a = 51, b = 136\nJ. a = 10, b = 0.85\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We are given the equation P = ar + bW and two data points from surveys.\nFor Survey 1: 170 = a(51) + b(136)\nFor Survey 2: 425 = a(68) + b(204)\n\nWe can solve this system of two linear equations with two unknowns (a and b). Let's try to simplify the equations by dividing by common factors.\nIn Survey 2, both 425, 68, and 204 are divisible by 17.\n425 / 17 = 25\n68 / 17 = 4\n204 / 17 = 12\nSo, Survey 2 simplifies to 25 = 4a + 12b.\n\nLet's see if Survey 1 can be simplified. Both 170 and 51 are divisible by 17.\n170 / 17 = 10\n51 / 17 = 3\nSo, Survey 1 can be written as 10 = 3a + 136b / 17. This does not simplify nicely.\n\nLet's re-examine the original equations:\n1) 170 = 51a + 136b\n2) 425 = 68a + 204b\n\nNotice that in equation 2, 425 = 17 * 25, 68 = 17 * 4, and 204 = 17 * 12. So, equation 2 is equivalent to 25 = 4a + 12b.\nIn equation 1, 170 = 17 * 10, 51 = 17 * 3. So, equation 1 is equivalent to 10 = 3a + (136/17)b = 3a + 8b.\n\nNow we have a simpler system of equations:\n1') 10 = 3a + 8b\n2') 25 = 4a + 12b\n\nLet's try to eliminate one variable. Multiply equation 1') by 4 and equation 2') by 3:\n4 * (10 = 3a + 8b)  => 40 = 12a + 32b\n3 * (25 = 4a + 12b) => 75 = 12a + 36b\n\nSubtract the first modified equation from the second:\n(75 - 40) = (12a - 12a) + (36b - 32b)\n35 = 4b\nb = 35/4 = 8.75\n\nSubstitute b = 8.75 into equation 1'):\n10 = 3a + 8(8.75)\n10 = 3a + 70\n3a = 10 - 70\n3a = -60\na = -20\n\nSo the values are a = -20 and b = 8.75. This corresponds to option H.\n\nLet's recheck if there was a simpler way to see this without solving the system.\nConsider option B: a = 2, b = 1.25\nSurvey 1: P = 2 * 51 + 1.25 * 136 = 102 + 170 = 272. This is not 170.\n\nConsider option F: a = 4, b = 1.5\nSurvey 1: P = 4 * 51 + 1.5 * 136 = 204 + 204 = 408. This is not 170.\n\nConsider option G: a = 3, b = 0.5\nSurvey 1: P = 3 * 51 + 0.5 * 136 = 153 + 68 = 221. This is not 170.\n\nConsider option E: a = 5, b = 2\nSurvey 1: P = 5 * 51 + 2 * 136 = 255 + 272 = 527. This is not 170.\n\nConsider option H: a = -20, b = 8.75\nSurvey 1: P = -20 * 51 + 8.75 * 136 = -1020 + 1190 = 170. This matches.\nSurvey 2: P = -20 * 68 + 8.75 * 204 = -1360 + 1785 = 425. This also matches.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{H}$.",
