    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_177",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Given that the cost of mimeographing x number of copies is C(x) = 0.005x + [(4500) / x], what is the number of copies that will minimize the cost?\n\nOptions: \nA. 2000 copies\nB. 500 copies\nC. 1200 copies\nD. 300 copies\nE. 700 copies\nF. 600 copies\nG. 1500 copies\nH. 949 copies\nI. 800 copies\nJ. 1000 copies\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To minimize the cost function C(x) = 0.005x + 4500/x, we need to find the value of x where the derivative of C(x) with respect to x is equal to zero.\n\nFirst, find the derivative of C(x):\nC'(x) = d/dx (0.005x + 4500x⁻¹)\nC'(x) = 0.005 - 4500x⁻²\nC'(x) = 0.005 - 4500/x²\n\nNext, set the derivative equal to zero and solve for x:\n0.005 - 4500/x² = 0\n0.005 = 4500/x²\nx² = 4500 / 0.005\nx² = 900000\nx = sqrt(900000)\nx = 948.68\n\nSince the number of copies must be an integer, we should choose the integer closest to 948.68. Looking at the options provided, 949 is the closest integer. In reality, we would also need to check the second derivative to confirm this is a minimum, but for multiple-choice questions of this nature, the critical point usually yields the correct answer.\n\nThe number of copies that will minimize the cost is approximately 949.\n\nComparing this value to the given options, option H, 949 copies, is the closest.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{H}$.",
