      "generated_answer": "The Rule of 72 is a simplified mathematical formula used to estimate the number of years it takes for an investment to double, given a fixed annual rate of interest. While often applied to investments, it can also be used for other situations involving exponential growth, such as population growth. Option H most comprehensively describes this application.\n\nThe most likely correct answer is **H**.",
