    "global index": "MMLUPro_economics_5639",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which is the best way to describe the AS curve in the long run?\n\nOptions: \nA. Always upward sloping because it follows the Law of Supply.\nB. Always downward sloping due to decreased demand over time.\nC. Always upward sloping due to the effects of inflation.\nD. Fluctuates between upward and downward sloping.\nE. Always vertical in the short run.\nF. Always downward sloping.\nG. Always vertical in the long run.\nH. Always horizontal.\nI. Fluctuates between vertical and horizontal.\nJ. Always horizontal due to constant supply.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The long-run aggregate supply (LRAS) curve is considered vertical. This is because in the long run, the economy's output is determined by its resources, technology, and institutions, not by the price level. Changes in the price level do not affect the potential output of the economy in the long run. Therefore, the LRAS curve is not upward or downward sloping, nor does it fluctuate. It is also incorrect to describe the short-run aggregate supply (SRAS) curve as always vertical, as the SRAS curve *is* generally upward sloping in the short run, reflecting sticky wages and prices. The LRAS curve being vertical is a fundamental concept in macroeconomics.\n\nThe best way to describe the AS curve in the long run is that it is always vertical. This position represents the economy's potential output, which is determined by factors of production and technology rather than the price level. Consequently, in the long run, changes in the aggregate price level do not alter the total output supplied by the economy.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{G}$.",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 183,
        "output_tokens": 218,
        "total_tokens": 401
      },
      "provider": "openrouter",
      "error": null
