    "global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6409",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is Gresham's Law?\n\nOptions: \nA. Bad money drives out good\nB. The value of money is directly proportional to its quantity\nC. Bad money increases the value of good money\nD. Good money drives out bad\nE. The quantity of money in circulation determines its value\nF. Money retains its value regardless of its condition\nG. Good and bad money circulate together in harmony\nH. The intrinsic value of money is less important than its nominal value\nI. Money has no intrinsic value\nJ. All money is equally desired\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Gresham's Law states that when two forms of currency are in circulation that are legally accepted at the same value, but one is intrinsically more valuable (e.g., contains more precious metal), the less valuable currency will be used in circulation, while the more valuable currency will be hoarded or exported. This is often summarized as \"bad money drives out good.\"\n\nThe most likely correct answer is **A**.\n\n\"Bad money drives out good\" is the classic statement of Gresham's Law. This means that if there are two types of currency in circulation, one perceived as \"bad\" (e.g., debased or of lower intrinsic value) and one as \"good\" (of higher intrinsic value), people will tend to spend the bad money and hoard or export the good money. This leaves the bad money to circulate in the economy. Options B and E are related to quantity theory, not Gresham's Law. Option D is the opposite of Gresham's Law.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{A}$.",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 175,
        "output_tokens": 214,
        "total_tokens": 389
      },
      "provider": "openrouter",
      "error": null
