      "generated_answer": "The coefficient of elasticity, in economics, measures the responsiveness of one variable to a change in another, usually a percentage change. Specifically, it is the percentage change in the dependent variable divided by the percentage change in the independent variable. This allows for a unit-free comparison of responsiveness across different scenarios.\n\nTherefore, the most likely correct answer is F.\n\nThe percentage change in the dependent variable divided by the percentage change in the independent variable.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
