    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Marginal cost always intersects average variable cost at\n\nOptions: \nA. the minimum of average total cost\nB. the point where average variable cost is equal to marginal cost\nC. the profit-maximizing quantity\nD. the maximum of average variable cost\nE. the point of equilibrium between supply and demand\nF. the point where marginal cost equals average total cost\nG. the minimum of average variable cost\nH. the point where average variable cost is less than marginal cost\nI. the minimum of marginal cost\nJ. the maximum of marginal cost\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is G. Marginal cost always intersects average variable cost at the minimum of average variable cost. This is a fundamental concept in microeconomics. When marginal cost is below average variable cost, it pulls the average down. When marginal cost is above average variable cost, it pulls the average up. Therefore, the point where they intersect must be the minimum of the average variable cost.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{G}$.",
