    "global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6053",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following are alternative names for the dependent variable (usually denoted by y) in linear regression analysis?\n\n(i) The regressand\n\n(ii) The regressor\n\n(iii) The explained variable\n\n(iv) The explanatory variable\n\nOptions: \nA. (ii), (iii), and (iv) only\nB. (i), (iii), and (iv) only\nC. (i) and (ii) only\nD. (i), (ii), and (iii) only\nE. (i) and (iv) only\nF. (ii) and (iv) only\nG. (i), (ii), (iii), and (iv)\nH. (ii) and (iii) only\nI. (i) and (iii) only\nJ. (iii) and (iv) only\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The question asks for alternative names for the dependent variable (y) in linear regression. Let's analyze each option:\n\n(i) The regressand: This is a standard alternative name for the dependent variable.\n(ii) The regressor: This is an alternative name for the independent variable (x), not the dependent variable.\n(iii) The explained variable: This accurately describes the dependent variable, as it is the variable being explained or predicted by the independent variables.\n(iv) The explanatory variable: This is an alternative name for the independent variable (x), not the dependent variable.\n\nTherefore, the correct alternative names for the dependent variable are (i) The regressand and (iii) The explained variable.\n\nLooking at the options:\nA. (ii), (iii), and (iv) only - Incorrect (includes regressors)\nB. (i), (iii), and (iv) only - Incorrect (includes explanatory variable)\nC. (i) and (ii) only - Incorrect (includes regressor)\nD. (i), (ii), and (iii) only - Incorrect (includes regressor)\nE. (i) and (iv) only - Incorrect (includes explanatory variable)\nF. (ii) and (iv) only - Incorrect (only includes regressors)\nG. (i), (ii), (iii), and (iv) - Incorrect (includes both regressors and explanatory variable)\nH. (ii) and (iii) only - Incorrect (includes regressor)\nI. (i) and (iii) only - Correct (includes regressand and explained variable)\nJ. (iii) and (iv) only - Incorrect (includes explanatory variable)\n\nThe correct answer is (i) and (iii) only.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
