  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_economics_5882",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Define poverty.\n\nOptions: \nA. Poverty is the lack of resources to secure basic life necessities.\nB. Poverty is the condition where a person has excessive wealth and resources.\nC. Poverty is the inability to afford a good standard of living.\nD. Poverty is the condition of having too little money to fulfill basic needs as society currently defines those needs.\nE. Poverty is the inability to purchase luxury items and services.\nF. Poverty is the state of living in a rural area without urban amenities.\nG. Poverty is the temporary lack of employment.\nH. Poverty is the state of being inferior in quality or insufficient in amount.\nI. Poverty is the condition of having an income that is less than the median income of a country.\nJ. Poverty is exclusively the state of not having access to education.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
