      "generated_answer": "The options A, C, D, and H all relate to a lack of resources or a low standard of living, which are core aspects of poverty. However, option D provides the most comprehensive and nuanced definition by acknowledging that basic needs are **society-defined**. This is crucial because what constitutes a basic need can vary across different societies and over time. While A and C are good definitions, they lack the societal context. H is too general. Option B describes wealth, E describes luxury, F describes a location, G describes a temporary situation, I describes relative poverty, and J describes one facet of disadvantage.\n\nThe most likely correct answer is $\\boxed{D}$.",
