    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The \"invisible hand\" concept, as described by Adam Smith, suggests that individuals acting in their own self-interest, within a competitive market, inadvertently promote the broader societal good. This societal good, in the context of resource allocation and economic efficiency, is best represented by the optimal use of scarce resources. Therefore, the public interest in this framework refers to the efficient allocation and utilization of these limited resources.\n\nThe correct answer is **E**.",
