production facilities.\nJ. Capital widening is when the overall investment in the economy increases without regard to the labor force, while capital deepening is when investment is focused on innovation rather than on increasing the capital per worker.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
