    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is meant by the \"double taxation\" problem in the corporate income tax system?\n\nOptions: \nA. Double taxation refers to applying two different types of taxes on the same income source\nB. Double taxation means that taxes are applied both to revenue and profits of a corporation\nC. Double taxation is when an individual is taxed twice on their personal income for the same tax year\nD. Double taxation refers to paying taxes twice in two different tax years\nE. Double taxation refers to the process of taxing imported goods twice\nF. Double taxation refers to companies paying the same tax in two different states\nG. Double taxation occurs when two or more shareholders are taxed for the same income\nH. Double taxation refers to paying both state and federal taxes\nI. Double taxation arises when a corporation is taxed for its earnings and also for the investments it makes with those earnings\nJ. Double taxation refers to the fact that some corporate income is taxed twice: once at the corporate level and again at the personal level when dividends are distributed to stockholders.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
