    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How many parameters will be required to be estimated in total for all equations of a standard form, unrestricted, tri-variate VAR(4), ignoring the intercepts?\n\nOptions: \nA. 6\nB. 9\nC. 16\nD. 12\nE. 4\nF. 3\nG. 48\nH. 24\nI. 36\nJ. 18\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "A standard form, unrestricted, tri-variate VAR(4) model for three variables $y_{1t}, y_{2t}, y_{3t}$ can be written as:\n$y_{1t} = c_1 + \\sum_{i=1}^{4} \\alpha_{11,i} y_{1,t-i} + \\sum_{i=1}^{4} \\alpha_{12,i} y_{2,t-i} + \\sum_{i=1}^{4} \\alpha_{13,i} y_{3,t-i} + \\epsilon_{1t}$\n$y_{2t} = c_2 + \\sum_{i=1}^{4} \\alpha_{21,i} y_{1,t-i} + \\sum_{i=1}^{4} \\alpha_{22,i} y_{2,t-i} + \\sum_{i=1}^{4} \\alpha_{23,i} y_{3,t-i} + \\epsilon_{2t}$\n$y_{3t} = c_3 + \\sum_{i=1}^{4} \\alpha_{31,i} y_{1,t-i} + \\sum_{i=1}^{4} \\alpha_{32,i} y_{2,t-i} + \\sum_{i=1}^{4} \\alpha_{33,i} y_{3,t-i} + \\epsilon_{3t}$\n\nWe have 3 equations (for the three variables).\nFor each equation, we have lag coefficients for each of the 3 variables, up to lag 4. So, for each equation, there are $3 \\times 4 = 12$ lag coefficients.\nSince there are 3 equations, the total number of lag coefficients to be estimated is $3 \\times 12 = 36$.\nThe question explicitly asks to ignore the intercepts, so we do not count $c_1, c_2, c_3$.\nTherefore, the total number of parameters to be estimated is 36.\n\nThe correct answer is G.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{G}$.",
