    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The autocovariance at lag $k$ for an MA(1) process $y_t = \\mu + \\epsilon_t + \\theta \\epsilon_{t-1}$ is given by:\n$\\gamma_k = \\begin{cases} \\sigma_\\epsilon^2(1+\\theta^2) & \\text{if } k=0 \\\\ \\sigma_\\epsilon^2 \\theta & \\text{if } k=1 \\\\ 0 & \\text{if } k > 1 \\end{cases}$\nIn this case, $\\mu=0$ and $\\theta=0.4$. We are looking for the autocovariance at lag 1, which is $\\gamma_1 = \\sigma_\\epsilon^2 \\theta$.\nThe question does not provide the disturbance variance $\\sigma_\\epsilon^2$. Therefore, it is not possible to determine the exact numerical value of the autocovariance at lag 1.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{J}$.",
