  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_economics_5741",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following assumptions are required to show the consistency, unbiasedness and efficiency of the OLS estimator?\n\ni) $E(u_t) = 0$\n\n\nii) $\\text{{Var}}(u_t) = \\sigma^2$\n\n\niii) $\\text{{Cov}}(u_t, u_{{t-j}}) = 0 \\forall j$\n\n\niv) $u_t \\sim N(0, \\sigma^2)$\n\nOptions: \nA. (i), (ii), (iii), and (iv)\nB. (i), (iii), and (iv) only\nC. (ii) and (iv) only\nD. (i), (ii), and (iii) only\nE. (ii) and (iii) only\nF. (i) and (ii) only\nG. (iii) and (iv) only\nH. (ii), (iii), and (iv) only\nI. (i) and (iv) only\nJ. (i) and (iii) only\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The Gauss-Markov theorem establishes the conditions under which the Ordinary Least Squares (OLS) estimator is the Best Linear Unbiased Estimator (BLUE). These conditions are related to the errors ($u_t$), not necessarily assuming normality.\n\n*   $E(u_t) = 0$: This is required for unbiasedness.\n*   $\\text{Var}(u_t) = \\sigma^2$: This assumption of homoscedasticity is needed for efficiency (specifically, for the standard errors to be calculated correctly and for OLS to be BLUE).\n*   $\\text{Cov}(u_t, u_{t-j}) = 0 \\forall j$: This assumption of no autocorrelation is needed for efficiency and for valid standard error calculations.\n*   $u_t \\sim N(0, \\sigma^2)$: This assumption of normality is *not* required for consistency, unbiasedness, or efficiency. It is only required for hypothesis testing and interval estimation in small samples.\n\nTherefore, assumptions (i), (ii), and (iii) are required for consistency, unbiasedness, and efficiency.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{D}$.",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 283,
        "output_tokens": 241,
        "total_tokens": 524
      },
