    "global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6186",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following are plausible approaches to dealing with a model that exhibits heteroscedasticity?\n\ni) Take logarithms of each of the variables\n\nii) Use suitably modified standard errors\n\niii) Use a generalised least squares procedure\n\niv) Add lagged values of the variables to the regression equation.\n\nOptions: \nA. (iii) and (iv) only\nB. (i), (iii), and (iv) only\nC. (i), (ii), and (iv) only\nD. (ii), (iii), and (iv) only\nE. (i) and (ii) only\nF. (i) and (iv) only\nG. (i) and (iii) only\nH. (ii) and (iv) only\nI. (i), (ii), (iii), and (iv)\nJ. (i), (ii), and (iii) only\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Heteroscedasticity means the variance of the error term is not constant.\n\n*   **Taking logarithms (i)** can sometimes stabilize the variance, making it a plausible approach.\n*   **Modified standard errors (ii)**, like heteroscedasticity-consistent standard errors (e.g., White standard errors), directly address the issue without changing the model's coefficient estimates themselves.\n*   **Generalized Least Squares (GLS) (iii)** is a method designed to handle non-constant error variances by transforming the data or the model.\n*   **Adding lagged values (iv)** is typically a strategy to address autocorrelation (serial correlation), not heteroscedasticity. While sometimes including lagged variables can indirectly affect the error structure, it's not a direct or primary method for dealing with heteroscedasticity itself.\n\nTherefore, (i), (ii), and (iii) are plausible approaches.\n\nThe correct answer is \\boxed{J}.",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 249,
        "output_tokens": 196,
