  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6113",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following statements are true concerning the acf and pacf?\n\n(i) The acf and pacf are often hard to interpret in practice\n\n(ii) The acf and pacf can be difficult to calculate for some data sets\n\n(iii) Information criteria represent an alternative approach to model order determination\n\n(iv) If applied correctly, the acf and pacf will always deliver unique model selections\n\nOptions: \nA. (i) and (ii) only\nB. (i) and (iii) only\nC. (iii) and (iv) only\nD. (ii), (iii), and (iv) only\nE. (ii) and (iii) only\nF. (i), (ii), (iii), and (iv)\nG. (i), (iii), and (iv) only\nH. (i) and (iv) only\nI. (ii) and (iv) only\nJ. (i), (ii), and (iii) only\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let's analyze each statement:\n\n**(i) The acf and pacf are often hard to interpret in practice:** This is generally true. While they provide valuable information, identifying clear patterns for specific ARMA model orders can be subjective and challenging, especially with noisy data.\n\n**(ii) The acf and pacf can be difficult to calculate for some data sets:** This is usually not the case. The ACF and PACF are standard statistical calculations that can be applied to most time series data. Difficulty might arise in interpretation, not calculation.\n\n**(iii) Information criteria represent an alternative approach to model order determination:** This is true. AIC, BIC, and other information criteria are widely used as objective methods to compare and select the best-fitting time series models by balancing goodness-of-fit with model complexity.\n\n**(iv) If applied correctly, the acf and pacf will always deliver unique model selections:** This is false. As mentioned in (i), ACF and PACF interpretation can be subjective, and it's possible for multiple model orders to seem plausible, or no clear order to emerge.\n\nBased on this analysis, statements (i) and (iii) are true. This corresponds to option B.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{B}$.",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 271,
        "output_tokens": 261,
        "total_tokens": 532
      },
      "provider": "openrouter",
      "error": null
    },
    "cost": null,
    "accuracy": null
  },
  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6118",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Suppose that 100 separate firms were tested to determine how many of them \"beat the market\" using a Jensen-type regression, and it is found that 3 fund managers significantly do so. Does this suggest prima facie evidence for stock market inefficiency?\n\nOptions: \nA. The results would be different if a different type of regression was used\nB. This suggests evidence for stock market efficiency, not inefficiency\nC. Yes\nD. In order to answer this question, you would need to test every fund manager trading in that market\nE. There is insufficient information given in the question to draw a conclusion about market efficiency.\nF. No\nG. The results are inconclusive without knowing the performance of the market as a whole\nH. It's impossible to draw conclusions based on the performance of only 100 firms\nI. This indicates that the majority of fund managers do not significantly beat the market\nJ. This suggests that only a small percentage of fund managers can beat the market\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "openai/gpt-4o-mini",
    "generated_result": {
