      "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is **F**.\n\nThe International Court of Justice (ICJ) addressed the accumulation theory in the Nicaragua case. In its ruling, the Court did not explicitly endorse the theory as presented by Nicaragua, and instead focused on the gravity of individual acts. While the ICJ acknowledged the cumulative effect of certain actions, it ultimately found that the individual attacks did not meet the threshold of an armed attack necessary to justify self-defense under Article 51 of the UN Charter. Therefore, the ICJ effectively dismissed the accumulation theory in its application to that case.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{F}$.",
