    "global index": "MMLUPro_law_1496",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A company created a new brand of pies. However, a study by the federal Food and Drug Administration revealed that the pies contain potentially harmful levels of nuts for some consumers with nut allergies. As a result, Congress enacted legislation prohibiting the shipment and sale of the pies across state lines. A state has a statute that regulates the shipment and sale of the pies within its territory. In light of the federal legislation prohibiting the shipment and sale of the pies across state lines, the state statute is probably\n\nOptions: \nA. constitutional, because it is within the state's police power.\nB. unconstitutional, because the federal law takes precedence in matters of public safety.\nC. constitutional, because the state has a compelling interest in protecting its citizens.\nD. unconstitutional, because it infringes on the rights of the pie company.\nE. constitutional, because Congress did not expressly preempt state legislation.\nF. constitutional, because the state has the right to regulate all commerce within its borders.\nG. constitutional, because Congress may not regulate an economic activity where both buyer and seller reside in the same state.\nH. unconstitutional, because it affects interstate commerce.\nI. unconstitutional, because the state cannot contradict federal regulations.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is **I. unconstitutional, because the state cannot contradict federal regulations.**\n\nThe Supremacy Clause of the U.S. Constitution states that federal laws are the supreme law of the land. When a valid federal law, such as the one prohibiting interstate shipment and sale of the pies, conflicts with a state law, the federal law prevails, and the state law becomes invalid. While states do have police powers and an interest in protecting citizens, these powers are limited by federal legislation when there is a conflict.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{I}$.",
      "success": true,
