    "global index": "MMLUPro_law_982",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Each year the state provides a number of non- interest-bearing loans andlor scholarships to candidates for the degree of L. L. B or J. D. at the state's law school. The applicable state statute limits eligibility to citizens of the United States and aliens seeking U. S. citizenship. A candidate for a J. D. degree at the state law school applied for one of the non-interest-bearing loans. Since he did not intend to seek U. S. citizenship, he was refused the loan for ineligibility under the state statute. In a suit by the candidate challenging the constitutionality of the state statute, he will\n\nOptions: \nA. lose, because the state has the right to limit eligibility for its programs.\nB. lose, because the statute promotes a compelling state interest.\nC. lose, because the statute is in accordance with the state's education policies.\nD. lose, because alienage classifications are not, per Se, unconstitutional under the Fourteenth Amendment's equal protection clause.\nE. win, because the statute infringes on the candidate's right to financial aid.\nF. win, because classifications by a state that are based on alienage are inherently suspect and subject to close judicial scrutiny.\nG. lose, because classifications by a state based on citizenship status are constitutional.\nH. win, because the statute is violative of the privileges or immunities clause of the Fourteenth Amendment.\nI. win, because the statute discriminates against those who choose not to pursue U.S. citizenship.\nJ. win, because the statute violates the candidate's right to equal treatment under the law.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
